    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628277\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 24th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628278\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 25th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628282\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 am</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19285325/invasion-of-the-body-snatchers-1956\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/XFhenyIpoGv2K3KB8IDRjWnsx2_lJuKA523JLgFmxLo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19285325/invasion-of-the-body-snatchers-1956\" target=\"\">Invasion of the Body Snatchers (1956)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1956</span>                                        <span>80mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Don Siegel</span>                                        <span>Starring Dana Wynter, Kevin McCarthy, Carolyn Jones, King Donovan, Larry Gates, Virginia Christine</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>* ON SALE 23rd SEPT *</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>In the sleepy Californian town of Santa Mira, strange happenings are afoot. Dr. Miles Bennell finds residents experiencing an epidemic of mass hysteria, imagining their relatives replaced by detached, emotionless copies. As Bennell gets closer to the horrifying truth - that the substitutions are part of an extraterrestrial invasion scheme and the copies are emerging from giant seed pods - the &#39;pod people&#39; begin to close in.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 12th October</div>                                                <li class=\"1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627567\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2585438/under-the-skin-2013\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/F24fbjJbE2rVTizUOs9544if2Ow786tep-HC8z4z0UM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2585438/under-the-skin-2013\" target=\"\">Under the Skin (2013)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2013</span>                                        <span>108mins</span>                                        <span>Switzerland, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jonathan Glazer</span>                                        <span>Starring Scarlett Johansson, Jeremy McWilliams, Lynsey Taylor Mackay</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>An alien entity inhabits the earthly form of a seductive young woman who combs the Scottish highways in search of the human prey it is here to plunder. It lures its isolated and forsaken male victims into an otherworldly dimension where they are stripped and consumed. But life in all its complexity starts to change the alien. It begins to see itself as 'she', as human, with tragic and terrifying consequences.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 12th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627566\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Monday 26th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627654\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617502/rogue-trooper\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/8JTQ0-VP0wY19dDrwisMzKkm4R0mPQFkkWcASEnMdiw.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617502/rogue-trooper\" target=\"\">Rogue Trooper</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Duncan Jones</span>                                        <span>Starring Aneurin Barnard, Matt Berry, Hayley Atwell, Jack Lowden</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/rogue-trooper-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Duncan Jones brings the beloved 2000 AD comic strip to life with an all-guns-blazing sci-fi animation, about a soldier in a dystopian future who is sent on an impossible mission.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Biochipped genetic soldiers, whose personalities can be downloaded should they fall on the battlefield, fight a futile, violent war across a chemically toxic landscape. Time is of the essence for their mission, but a raft of horrors await them. Fast and funny, Rogue Trooper is skilfully directed by Jones (Moon and Source Code), who gives this terrific British indie the feel of a Hollywood blockbuster.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 12th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/rogue-trooper-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:35 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13082687/jennifers-body\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/13082687.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13082687/jennifers-body\" target=\"\">Jennifer&#039;s Body</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2009</span>                                        <span>102mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Teen / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Karyn Kusama</span>                                        <span>Starring Megan Fox, Adam Brody, Amanda Seyfried</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>&quot;She&#39;s evil&hellip; and not just high school evil.&rdquo;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A demon possesses high-school It-girl Jennifer (Megan Fox) after she is kidnapped and sacrificed in a failed occult ritual. Bloodthirsty, she seeks revenge through any man who crosses her path, but is challenged when her best friend, Needy (Amanda Seyfried), won&acute;t stand idly by as the body-count rises.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Campy, funny, horrific and truly impressive. After initially receiving mixed critical reception, Jennifer&acute;s Body has become a horror and teen cult-classic as queer and female audiences have reclaimed the title. Ahead of its time, the film is still referenced in Halloween costumes, fan-theories, and video edits as audiences are hungrier than ever for the iconic maneater, Jennifer Check!&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><em><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Jennifer&acute;s Body is featured as part of MANEATERS, a season exploring the female supernatural on screen. The season is presented with the National Film and Television School&rsquo;s Film Studies, Programming and Curation MA.</span></em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 13th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627504\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 30th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627682\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3847488/funeral-parade-presents-a-nightmare-on-elm-street-2-freddys-revenge\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/bQD0JECPMa2Ns8t_Z8I2-TBpOvWF3SWfae1ovExKRi0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3847488/funeral-parade-presents-a-nightmare-on-elm-street-2-freddys-revenge\" target=\"\">Funeral Parade presents A Nightmare on Elm Street 2: Freddy&#039;s Revenge</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1985</span>                                        <span>87mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jack Sholder</span>                                        <span>Starring Robert Englund, Mark Patton, Kim Myers</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><em><strong>Just in time for Spooky Season, Funeral Parade is proud to present A Nightmare on Elm Street 2: Freddy&rsquo;s Revenge, a queer-coded slasher classic.</strong></em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The man of your dreams is BACK! That&rsquo;s right, Freddy Krueger has returned to stalk Elm Street once again &ndash; and this time he&rsquo;s enlisting teenager Jesse Walsh to help carry out his evil deeds. Freddy intends to possess Jesse&rsquo;s body in order to take his bloody revenge on the teenage population of Springwood, Ohio. Will Jesse be able to resist him? A Nightmare on Elm Street 2: Freddy&rsquo;s Revenge has become infamous for its homoerotic subtext and features an iconic performance from Mark Patton as slasher cinema&rsquo;s first male &ldquo;scream queen&rdquo;.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>With intro from film curator Sarah Cleary.</em></strong></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 13th October</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627766\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617503/the-history-of-concrete\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/dPo-SXqTUnoMPZX-yz91_qGUDbtG6YYFyz14vsJzS1M.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617503/the-history-of-concrete\" target=\"\">The History of Concrete</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>101mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Wilson</span>                                                                            </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/history-of-concrete-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Having attended a Hallmark movie workshop, John Wilson applies his learnings to a documentary about concrete, albeit with a dryly funny and deceptively understated tone.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>After finding himself with too much time on his hands, documentarian Wilson attends a workshop on how to make Hallmark romcoms. It inspires him to apply the formula to a film investigating the story of concrete. Infused with Wilson&rsquo;s trademark curiosity and wit, the film project introduces him to a variety of unusual people and places. The result is a wry and humane meditation on the modern world.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>These&nbsp;screenings will be presented with Descriptive Subtitles.&nbsp;</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 13th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/history-of-concrete-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 15th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/history-of-concrete-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617504/queer-edward-ii\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/TwxTTprFTMCY-AN8k3I6sY2SYaXa9nK00X19HNmp8Pc.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617504/queer-edward-ii\" target=\"\">Queer Edward II</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>95mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Theo Rollason</span>                                        <span>Starring Derek Jarman, Tilda Swinton, Nigel Terry</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/fox-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>This all-archival tour de force takes us behind the scenes of Derek Jarman&rsquo;s Edward II, set against the backdrop of the anti-LGBTQIA+ legislation of 1980s Britain.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>This all-archival tour de force takes us behind the scenes of Derek Jarman&rsquo;s Edward II, set against the backdrop of the anti-LGBTQIA+ legislation of 1980s Britain. In 1991, Jarman started production on Edward II, just as queer life in the UK was under renewed threat from the British government. Seamus McGarvey captured all the drama on set in a previously unseen treasure trove of behind-the-scenes footage. Queer Edward II masterfully reanimates this archive as a vigorous and radical reflection on the power of art as protest.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 13th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/queer-edward-ii-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617370/mikey-and-nicky\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/iuutnaDDYpP-FNVXgbLarL3r3BElajkx4A6Iknjajz8.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617370/mikey-and-nicky\" target=\"\">Mikey and Nicky</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1976</span>                                        <span>106mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Elaine May</span>                                        <span>Starring Peter Falk, John Cassavetes, Ned Beatty</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong><em><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\">Our performance on 14th October is presented with an introduction by </span><a href=\"https://x.com/christinalefou\"><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\">Christina Newland</span></a></em></strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\nElaine May crafted a gangster film like no other in the nocturnal odyssey Mikey and Nicky, capitalising on the chemistry between frequent collaborators John Cassavetes and Peter Falk by casting them together as small-time mobsters whose lifelong relationship has turned sour. Set over the course of one night, this restless drama finds Nicky (Cassavetes) holed up in a hotel after the boss he stole money from puts a hit out on him. Terrified, he calls on Mikey (Falk), the one person he thinks can save him. Scripted to match the live-wire energy of its stars&mdash;alongside supporting players Ned Beatty, Joyce Van Patten, and Carol Grace&mdash;and inspired by real-life characters from May&rsquo;s own childhood, this unbridled portrait of male friendship turned tragic is an unsung masterpiece of American cinema.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><strong><em>Our performance on 14th October is featured as part of Gangsters Have Feelings Too, a season exploring the sensitive gangster film. The season is presented with the National Film and Television School&rsquo;s Film Studies, Programming and Curation MA.</em></strong></span></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 14th October</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627573\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 6th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628286\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">9:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617505/the-blood-countess\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/6jAKab8PKtzpX2DOrAEPp25IUalZOYXOSTYaWaC32qc.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617505/the-blood-countess\" target=\"\">The Blood Countess</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>119mins</span>                                        <span>Austria, Germany, Luxembourg</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Ulrike Ottinger</span>                                        <span>Starring Isabelle Huppert, Birgit Minichmayr, Thomas Schubert</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/fox-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\nTickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/blood-countess-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong><em>Isabelle Huppert dazzles as the Blood Countess in this delightful and high-camp gothic fantasy from visionary filmmaker Ulrike Ottinger.</em></strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>After awakening from a long slumber, the Blood Countess embarks on a quest, with her devoted maid and trusty pet bat in tow, to search for an ancient text that could cause the demise of her vampire realm. Based on the legend of Countess Elizabeth B&aacute;thory, Huppert perfectly embodies the role of the bloodthirsty seductress who reigns over present-day Vienna.</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nGerman and French Language with English subtitles</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 14th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/blood-countess-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617508/it-gets-worse\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/pcrzVi329Hvvpx4sWyHZp8LHUgsRLrkHe38ba5J_st0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617508/it-gets-worse\" target=\"\">It Gets Worse</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>69mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Mounia Akl</span>                                        <span>Starring Leo Reich, Emily Fairn, Olive Gray</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/it-gets-worse-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Leo Reich&rsquo;s new series turns the struggles of young Londoners into its playground, mining a generation&rsquo;s problems for biting, clever comedy.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Ethan, Abi and Sam, inseparable friends in their mid-20s, are forced into real adulthood when eviction looms. Razor-sharp and witty, It Gets Worse skewers a generation stuck between housing crisis, humiliating jobs and messy relationships, while savouring the joy of youth in one of the buzziest cities in the world. It&rsquo;s anchored by standout performances from the three leads, alongside unforgettable cameos from the likes of Lena Dunham and Andrew Scott.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 14th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/it-gets-worse-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">9:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617509/the-story-of-documentary-film-the-1990s\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/9ZG7RE2mY9pt3nE1HTYJHcmxojGMmjT53hK5fyfvuOo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617509/the-story-of-documentary-film-the-1990s\" target=\"\">The Story of Documentary Film (The 1990s)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Mark Cousins</span>                                                                            </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/story-of-documentary-film-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>This fascinating chapter from Mark Cousins&rsquo; epic essay on the history of documentary chronicles a decade of formal reinvention and mainstream success.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Cousins, the creator of the groundbreaking The Story of Film: A New Generation and Women Make Film, trains his distinctive film-historian lens on the evolution of documentary. The result is a rich tapestry of landmark works and underappreciated gems. In this illuminating chapter, he guides us through the 1990s, a decade of filmmakers exploring bodies, spirituality, labour, war and politics, against the backdrop of rising commercial interest in the form.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 15th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/story-of-documentary-film-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617510/the-unknown\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/x31K17oStTPxv985BtoUDctkEY8Q0ipT4NetJc_rkM0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617510/the-unknown\" target=\"\">The Unknown</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>140mins</span>                                        <span>France</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Arthur Harari</span>                                        <span>Starring Léa Seydoux, Niels Schneider, Valérie Dréville</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/default.asp?BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::permalink=unknown-lff26&amp;BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::context_id=\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Mesmerising, stimulating and unsettling, Niels Schneider and L&eacute;a Seydoux star in this body-swap tale that grapples with the existential implications of being trapped inside someone else&rsquo;s physical being.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>David, a withdrawn photographer, meets a mysterious woman at a party. The two share a sexual encounter, only for David to wake up the morning after in the woman&rsquo;s body. Arthur Harari&rsquo;s (co-writer of Anatomy of a Fall) vertiginous, occasionally harrowing and ultimately rewarding ride eschews straightforward resolution in favour of a reflection on the aftermath of severing the link between body and mind.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>French Language with English subtitles</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 15th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/unknown-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:55 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617511/the-face-of-horror\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/bJ8CVkduXPzJXJZNlrgDwJowx5KwmT1OcTxf9eZK3Bk.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617511/the-face-of-horror\" target=\"\">The Face of Horror</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Anna Biller</span>                                        <span>Starring Jonah Hauer-King, Kristine Froseth, Ellie Bamber, Bella Heathcote</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/face-of-horror-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>In this stunning, blood-soaked homage to Technicolor horror films, a woman in medieval England rises from the grave to wreak revenge on her husband.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Returning as a ghost after a cruel betrayal results in her death, Eleanor and her sister deliver bloody vengeance on the man who took her life and murdered their father. Anna Biller, writer-director of The Love Witch, here delivers a rich visual feast. Gloriously shot on 35mm, this supernatural Gothic melodrama vibrantly brings 14th-century England to life.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 15th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/face-of-horror-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 17th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/face-of-horror-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617246/weapons\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31617246.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617246/weapons\" target=\"\">Weapons</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2025</span>                                        <span>129mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Supernatural / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Zach Cregger</span>                                        <span>Starring Julia Garner, Josh Brolin, Alden Ehrenreich</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When all but one child from the same class mysteriously vanish on the same night at exactly the same time, a community is left questioning who or what is behind their disappearance.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 15th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627507\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">9:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617512/too-many-beasts\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/JL9fVEd3B4ybF3JVwoWqdhmhTnF0TGNWly7Tnhrrh4w.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617512/too-many-beasts\" target=\"\">Too Many Beasts</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>95mins</span>                                        <span>France</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Sarah Arnold</span>                                        <span>Starring Alexis Manenti, Ella Rumpf, Vincent Dedienne</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/too-many-beasts-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>In this deliciously unhinged mash-up of rural thriller and dark comedy, enormous wild boars create havoc in a small French town.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Farmers and hunters are openly at war in the rural town of S&eacute;rieux. Wild boars are ruining crops and putting everyone on edge. When a local farmer mysteriously disappears, gendarme Fulda is put on the case. As he reluctantly teams up with psychologist St&eacute;phane, the investigation gradually spirals out of control, and so does this offbeat and absurdly funny comedy.</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nFrench Language with English subtitles</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/too-many-beasts-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/27195258/i-know-what-you-did-last-summer\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/27195258.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/27195258/i-know-what-you-did-last-summer\" target=\"\">I Know What You Did Last Summer</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1997</span>                                        <span>102mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Teen / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jim Gillespie</span>                                        <span>Starring Sarah Michelle Gellar, Freddie Prinze Jr., Jennifer Love Hewitt, Ryan Phillippe, Freddie Prinze Jr, Johnny Galecki, Bridgette Wilson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Four young friends bound by a tragic accident are reunited when they find themselves being stalked by a hook-wielding maniac in their small seaside town.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627586\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617514/mouse\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/RQvT5LPfnLkEvIQjJz95nuodQPGjtHLD7dP2t6SAEbM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617514/mouse\" target=\"\">Mouse</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Alex Thompson|Kelly O'Sullivan</span>                                        <span>Starring Katherine Mallen Kupferer, Sophie Okonedo, Chloe Coleman</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/mouse-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Katherine Mallen Kupferer and Sophie Okonedo excel in this moving drama about facing up to life in the aftermath of a tragedy.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Lifelong friends Callie and Minnie are like ying and yang: one loud and popular, the other shy and quiet. Abruptly forced out from her friend&rsquo;s shadow, it&rsquo;s finally time for Minnie to figure out who she is on her own terms. Kupferer and Okonedo&rsquo;s performances drive this beautiful film that&rsquo;s guaranteed to have audiences alternating between crying and laughing out loud.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/mouse-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3639373/the-others\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/4jHH-ED_zRT-bPnXIiwjgUfcLuyRCLxvj9pvyopwOb0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3639373/the-others\" target=\"\">The Others</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2001</span>                                        <span>104mins</span>                                        <span>Spain, USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Mystery</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Alejandro Amenábar</span>                                        <span>Starring Nicole Kidman, Christopher Eccleston, Fionnula Flanagan</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Academy Award® winner Nicole Kidman (Best Actress, The Hours, 2003) delivers an unforgettable performance in this gothic supernatural thriller. In 1945, Grace (Kidman) and her two children wait for her husband's return from the war, living an unusually isolated existence behind the locked doors and drawn curtains of a secluded mansion in Jersey. Three mysterious new servants arrive and it becomes chillingly clear that there is far more to this house than can be seen, and Grace finds herself in a terrifying fight to save her children and preserve her sanity. Acclaimed by critics, the unpredictable twists and turns of this compelling psychological horror classic will keep you on the edge of your seat.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627585\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 21st October</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627611\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617515/godzilla-minus-zero\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/E7kiDBxKFZrXGyl-MITx6N7Gj5lE1q_92mCt5hC6FkY.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617515/godzilla-minus-zero\" target=\"\">Godzilla Minus Zero</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>135mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Takashi Yamazaki</span>                                        <span>Starring Ryunosuke Kamiki, Minami Hamabe, Yuki Yamada</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/godzilla-minus-zero-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>The sequel to Takashi Yamazaki&rsquo;s acclaimed 2023 film is a true cinematic spectacle that&rsquo;s sure to grip fans of Godzilla, as well as newcomers to the franchise.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Japan, 1949. Pilot Kōichi, his wife Noriko and adoptive daughter Akiko are attempting from recover from Godzilla&rsquo;s recent attacks. But just as everything seems settled, a new danger emerges. Meanwhile, at the bottom of the sea, something is stirring. The first Japanese film to be shot for IMAX, Godzilla Minus Zero combines high-octane thrills with more than a little heart.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Japanese Language with English subtitles</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/godzilla-minus-zero-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617470/halloween-1978-halloween-ii-1981-double-feature\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/e66m6qGkWCuuH0z3TPi4P3DpPjWrz2S_gOW0q-AO0Gg.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617470/halloween-1978-halloween-ii-1981-double-feature\" target=\"\">Halloween (1978) + Halloween II (1981) • Double Feature</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1978</span>                                        <span>183mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Carpenter|Rick Rosenthal</span>                                        <span>Starring Jamie Lee Curtis, Donald Pleasence, The Shape</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>HALLOWEEN (1978):&nbsp;Fifteen years after murdering his sister on Halloween Night 1963, Michael Myers escapes from a mental hospital and returns to the small town of Haddonfield, Illinois to kill again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>HALLOWEEN II (1981):&nbsp;After failing to kill stubborn survivor Laurie and taking a bullet or six from former psychiatrist Dr. Sam Loomis, Michael Myers has followed Laurie to the Haddonfield Memorial Hospital, where she&rsquo;s been admitted for Myers&rsquo; attempt on her life. The institution proves to be particularly suited to serial killers, however, as Myers cuts, stabs and slashes his way through hospital staff to reach his favourite victim.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Presented with a 10-15 minute break between features</em></strong></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627583\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617516/the-idiots\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/giUZzcTq8XHevmkyrtkiVKG2yZ7GOjqXIoqRHAVrL88.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617516/the-idiots\" target=\"\">The Idiot(s)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>118mins</span>                                        <span>Germany, Poland</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Małgorzata Szumowska|Michał Englert</span>                                        <span>Starring Aimee Lou Wood, Johnny Flynn, Vicky Krieps</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/idiots-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Aimee Lou Wood and Johnny Flynn are superb as Anna and Fyodor Dostoevsky in Małgorzata Szumowska and Michał Englert&rsquo;s acerbic and joyful period film.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Anna Dostoevsky loves her husband Fyodor. Fyodor loves his wife, but he also loves gambling and booze. Living in self-imposed exile in Germany, Fyodor&rsquo;s biggest obstacle to creative progress is himself. Anna tries desperately to rid him of his procrastination so he can deliver a new novel and they can avoid destitution. Sending up the myth of the male genius, The Idiot(s) is also a beautiful love story about the writer and the wife that saved him.</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nEnglish and French Language with English subtitles</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/idiots-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23819063/halloween-h20-20-years-later\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/wZlyLMi_piVvlJuPlE_P8YjRL083F1m8Q9VffNHw-BQ.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23819063/halloween-h20-20-years-later\" target=\"\">Halloween H20: 20 Years Later</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1998</span>                                        <span>86mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Steve Miner</span>                                        <span>Starring Michelle Williams, Jamie Lee Curtis, Joseph Gordon-Levitt, Josh Hartnett, Adam Arkin, L.L. Cool J</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>20 Years after escaping her brother Michael Myers's attacks, Laurie Strode, now the dean of a Northern California private school with an assumed name, must battle the Shape one last time, as the life of her own son hangs in the balance.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 16th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627584\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">9:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617517/wildwood\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/x5cyqxr7wCN4Ere1gFwWAGIhbTRe975y-J8HMp99kmo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617517/wildwood\" target=\"\">Wildwood</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>132mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Travis Knight</span>                                        <span>Starring Peyton Elizabeth Lee, Jacob Tremblay, Carey Mulligan, Mahershala Ali, Angela Bassett</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/wildwood-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>A forest inhabited by magical beings is the setting for this epic stop-motion saga from LAIKA Studios.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>When her baby brother is kidnapped by a large flock of crows, Prue hotfoots it to a local forest where a wondrous world of mystery and peril awaits. This breathtaking, hugely ambitious new film from LAIKA Studios (Coraline, Kubo and the Two Strings) is a masterpiece of stop-motion storytelling on an epic scale and quite unlike anything previously seen.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 17th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/wildwood-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 am</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2505/scream-2\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/2505.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2505/scream-2\" target=\"\">Scream 2</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1997</span>                                        <span>122mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Wes Craven</span>                                        <span>Starring Courteney Cox, David Arquette, Jada Pinkett Smith, Neve Campbell</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Sydney (Neve Campbell) and tabloid reporter Gale Weathers (Courteney Cox) survived the events of the first \"Scream,\" but their nightmare isn't over. When two college students are murdered at a sneak preview of \"Stab,\" a movie based on the events from the first film, it's clear a copycat killer is on the loose. Sydney and Gail, as well as fellow survivors Deputy Dewey (David Arquette) and Randy (Jamie Kennedy) have to find out who is behind this new murder spree, before they all end up dead.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 17th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627588\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:35 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617518/paper-tiger\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/k_Y18jBFgenh0qqwqXafkXmLrnEFSln5cZaazGBgDjQ.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617518/paper-tiger\" target=\"\">Paper Tiger</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>114mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by James Gray</span>                                        <span>Starring Scarlett Johansson, Adam Driver, Miles Teller</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/paper-tiger-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>James Gray goes back to his roots with this tense and atmospheric thriller, set in 1980s New York, which finds two brothers becoming embroiled with the Russian mafia.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Irwin Pearl (Miles Teller, on top form) is an engineer and family man living in Queens. When his brother, a showboating ex-police officer (a magnetic Adam Driver), enlists him for a high paying job, things rapidly take a turn for the worse. Channelling the spirit of Sidney Lumet and Michael Mann, Gray&rsquo;s own, distinctive directorial style is on full display in this instant classic of American crime cinema.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 17th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/paper-tiger-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/24271045/scream-3\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/24271045.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/24271045/scream-3\" target=\"\">Scream 3</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2000</span>                                        <span>117mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Wes Craven</span>                                        <span>Starring Courteney Cox, Courteney Cox Arquette, David Arquette, Deon Richmond, Jenny McCarthy, Neve Campbell, Parker Posey, Patrick Dempsey</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>As bodies begin dropping around the set of 'STAB 3', a movie sequel based on the gruesome Woodsboro killings, Sidney Prescott and the other survivors are once again drawn into a game of a horror movie mayhem.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 17th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627589\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617471/scream-4\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/YeM9Q37rRtja8u0qhIh9GkE8J5LOWZUcibp3fH7auY8.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617471/scream-4\" target=\"\">Scream 4</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2011</span>                                        <span>111mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Wes Craven</span>                                        <span>Starring Neve Campbell, David Arquette, Courteney Cox</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Fifteen years after the original Woodsboro murders, Sidney Prescott returns home to promote her new book about surviving trauma, only for a new Ghostface killer to emerge, targeting a new group of teens.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 17th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627590\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617519/your-mother-your-mother-your-mother\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/6FOtxr_8BithaerGltEkHl-8kxS4eea6Fy6QAleWNho.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617519/your-mother-your-mother-your-mother\" target=\"\">Your Mother Your Mother Your Mother</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>111mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Bassam Tariq</span>                                        <span>Starring Mahershala Ali, John Cho, Laith Nakli, Adia , Giancarlo Esposito</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/your-mother-your-mother-your-mother-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Bassam Tariq follows Mogul Mowgli (LFF 2020) with this gripping, inventive thriller, featuring a commanding central performance by Oscar winner Mahershala Ali.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>An assassin and father of three, Latif&rsquo;s life is turned upside down when his wife dies. He struggles to balance his two very different worlds, but when a hit goes south and as forces close in around him, he sets off on a desperate journey to protect his children. Amid all the mayhem, Tariq&rsquo;s stylish and exhilarating thriller offers a tender portrait of grief and fatherhood, and a testament to maintaining one&rsquo;s faith.</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nEnglish and Arabic Language with English Subtitles<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis&nbsp;screening&nbsp;will be presented with Descriptive Subtitles and will have Audio Description available on request.&nbsp;<br />\r\n<br />\r\nContent Warning: Contains scenes of graphic violence or injury.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 18th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/your-mother-your-mother-your-mother-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617520/club-kid\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/iegNjMKPCHUNVgODTEE5d5RbOq5OzmNQIUXS37xZyhk.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617520/club-kid\" target=\"\">Club Kid</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>122mins</span>                                                                                <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jordan Firstman</span>                                        <span>Starring Jordan Firstman, Reggie Absolom, Diego Calva, Cara Delevingne, Kirby Howell-Baptise</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/club-kid-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>A jaded New York club promoter finds his messy lifestyle upended by the discovery that he has a son, in Jordan Firstman&rsquo;s hilarious feature directorial debut.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>A decade of drinking, drugs and clubs is finally starting to take its toll on Peter. The unexpected arrival of an infant son means it&rsquo;s finally time for him to get his life together. How hard can it be? The perfect skewering of millennial malaise that is also deeply touching, it&rsquo;s easy to see why Club Kid was one of the most talked-about films at Cannes this year.</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis&nbsp;screening&nbsp;will be presented with Descriptive Subtitles.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nContent Warning: Contains flashing images, scenes of drug use and sex, and themes of suicide.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 18th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/club-kid-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:50 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617521/the-debut\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/jFPSG-QdrJDMyYQggvylrdS2fS4tJDAvTjuYH4JKkpE.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617521/the-debut\" target=\"\">The Debut</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>105mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>LFF</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jesse Eisenberg</span>                                        <span>Starring Julianne Moore, Paul Giamatti, Halle Bailey, Jesse Eisenberg, Cara Buono</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Tickets Are Only Available via BFI London Film Festival Website from Tuesday 17&nbsp;September 2026&nbsp;10:00am: <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/debut-lff26\">Click Here To Book</a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>For LFF 2026&rsquo;s curtain call, writer-director Jesse Eisenberg delivers a rapturous and raucously funny love letter to community theatre, featuring a luminous lead performance by Julianne Moore.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Quiet housewife Mona has become a supporting role in her own life; her husband barely acknowledges her presence and their children are on the cusp of fleeing the nest. So when, on an impulse, she auditions for a local production of an original musical, Mona suddenly finds herself in the spotlight when she is cast in a leading role, as Miss Danielle. However, she is unprepared for the theatrical hurricane that is Jerry, her enigmatic director and the &lsquo;biggest name in New Jersey community theatre&rsquo;. As she continues to be creatively pushed by him, Mona finds herself going to extreme lengths to unlock her character. The Debut once again finds the perfect balance between humour and drama that Eisenberg delivered with his previous films A Real Pain (LFF 2024) and When You Finish Saving the World. It&rsquo;s both sparklingly witty and laugh-out-loud funny, while every scene works to build on the emotional undercurrents and heartbreaking revelations that make the characters so credible. This time, Eisenberg&rsquo;s talents even stretch to writing the songs for the fictional stage musical. Moore is in her element, giving one of her finest performances, while Paul Giamatti&rsquo;s Jerry continues his run from The Holdovers as the master of dramedy. Ultimately, The Debut is an elegant and intelligent coming-of-older-age story about how it&rsquo;s never too late to find our true selves, and the redemptive powers of community and art. Take your seats... It&rsquo;s showtime!</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis&nbsp;screening&nbsp;will be presented with Descriptive Subtitles and will have Audio Description available on request.&nbsp;</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 18th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://whatson.bfi.org.uk/lff/Online/article/debut-lff26\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3084554/the-wicker-man-the-final-cut\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3084554.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3084554/the-wicker-man-the-final-cut\" target=\"\">The Wicker Man - The Final Cut</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1973</span>                                        <span>94mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Robin Hardy</span>                                        <span>Starring Christopher Lee, Diane Cilento, Edward Woodward</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A puritan police sergeant arrives in a Scottish island village in search of a missing girl, who the pagan locals claim never existed.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 19th October</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627599\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23838830/urban-legend\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/zm3rb5bne84vmLigxeWPNr8er5YnLK8x2Syctmpq328.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23838830/urban-legend\" target=\"\">Urban Legend</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1998</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Teen / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jamie Blanks</span>                                        <span>Starring Robert Englund, Jared Leto, Joshua Jackson, Rebecca Gayheart, Tara Reid, Alicia Witt</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When a series of murders take place in and around her university, Natalie begins to suspect that the deaths are inspired by various urban legends.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 19th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627601\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19522496/abbott-and-costello-meet-frankenstein\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/uCMJny5PhQBBKlRuwdwhOf3znW3sx1Nj65IWLDZsdDs.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19522496/abbott-and-costello-meet-frankenstein\" target=\"\">Abbott and Costello Meet Frankenstein</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1948</span>                                        <span>83mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Charles Barton</span>                                        <span>Starring Bud Abbott, Lou Costello, Lon Chaney Jr., Bela Lugosi, Glenn Strange, Lenore Aubert</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>* ON SALE 23rd SEP *</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The popular comedy team of the 1940s and 1950s, Bud Abbott and Lou Costello, goes up against Universal Studios&rsquo;s monsters in this zany spoof. Dracula (Bela Lugosi), the Wolf Man (Lon Chaney Jr.), and Frankenstein&rsquo;s Monster (Glenn Strange) all make memorable appearances in this horror comedy mashup, which manages to do justice to both genres―a feat frequently attempted but rarely achieved.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 19th October</div>                                                <li class=\"1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627596\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/24558830/frankenstein-1931-and-the-bride-of-frankenstein-1935\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/gFl_3YTaD3xLddaZT1JG0lyYJIxnHlyMFdazaR42u6Y.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/24558830/frankenstein-1931-and-the-bride-of-frankenstein-1935\" target=\"\">Frankenstein (1931) and The Bride of Frankenstein (1935)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1931</span>                                        <span>145mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Movie Marathons</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by James Whale</span>                                        <span>Starring Boris Karloff, Elsa Lanchester, Colin Clive, Valerie Hobson, Ernest Thesiger, E. E. Clive</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>FRANKENSTEIN (1931): Henry Frankenstein pieces together body parts in the hope of bringing a human-like creature to life. The mad scientist&rsquo;s dreams are shattered by his monstrous creation awakening with rage to a world that hates and fears him.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>THE BRIDE OF FRANKENSTEIN (1935): Dr. Frankenstein and his monster both turn out to be alive after being attacked by an angry mob. The now-chastened scientist attempts to escape his past, but a former mentor forces him to assist with the creation of a new creature.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Presented with a 10-minute break between features.</em></strong></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 19th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627595\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/618697/carrie\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/618697.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/618697/carrie\" target=\"\">Carrie</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1976</span>                                        <span>99mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Brian De Palma</span>                                        <span>Starring Sissy Spacek, Piper Laurie, Amy Irving</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In this chilling adaptation of Stephen King's horror novel, withdrawn and sensitive teen Carrie White (Sissy Spacek) faces taunting from classmates at school and abuse from her fanatically pious mother (Piper Laurie) at home. When strange occurrences start happening around Carrie, she begins to suspect that she has supernatural powers. Invited to the prom by the empathetic Tommy Ross (William Katt), Carrie tries to let her guard down, but things eventually take a dark and violent turn.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 20th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627606\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">1:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9899349/the-witch\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/9899349.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9899349/the-witch\" target=\"\">The Witch</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2015</span>                                        <span>93mins</span>                                        <span>Canada, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Robert Eggers</span>                                        <span>Starring Anya Taylor-Joy, Kate Dickie, Ralph Ineson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><em><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\"><strong>Featuring an intro from Writer/Director Robert Eggers on Tuesday 20th October</strong></span></em><br />\r\n<br />\r\nIn 1630 New England, panic and despair envelops a farmer, his wife and their children when youngest son Samuel suddenly vanishes. The family blames Thomasin, the oldest daughter who was watching the boy at the time of his disappearance. With suspicion and paranoia mounting, twin siblings Mercy and Jonas suspect Thomasin of witchcraft, testing the clan&#39;s faith, loyalty and love to one another.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 20th October</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627610\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1578578/seven\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1578578.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1578578/seven\" target=\"\">Seven</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1995</span>                                        <span>127mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by David Fincher</span>                                        <span>Starring Morgan Freeman, Brad Pitt, John Doe</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>GLUTTONY. GREED. SLOTH. WRATH. PRIDE. LUST. ENVY.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Two cops (Brad Pitt and Morgan Freeman) track a brilliant and elusive killer who orchestrates a string of horrific murders, each kill targeting a practitioner of one of the Seven Deadly Sins. Gwyneth Paltrow also stars in this acclaimed thriller set in a dour, drizzly city sick with pain and blight. David Fincher (Fight Club, Zodiac, The Curious Case of Benjamin Button) guides the action - physical, mental and spiritual - with a sure understanding of what terrifies us, right up to a stunning denouement that will rip the scar tissue off the most hardened soul.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>The 4K restoration of &ldquo;Se7en&rdquo; was completed at Warner Bros. Discovery&rsquo;s Motion Picture Imaging and sourced from the original camera negative. The restoration was overseen by David Fincher.&nbsp;</em></strong></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 20th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627603\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19285657/the-innocents-1961\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/YslOcxKq_mg21ryLcJPUivX9k2LTFbot3mwZj89B2cw.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19285657/the-innocents-1961\" target=\"\">The Innocents (1961)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1961</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Supernatural / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jack Clayton</span>                                        <span>Starring Deborah Kerr, Peter Wyngarde, Megs Jenkins</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In Victorian England, the uncle of orphaned niece Flora and nephew Miles hires Miss Giddens as governess to raise the children at his estate with total independence and authority. Soon after her arrival, Miss Giddens comes to believe that the spirits of the former governess Miss Jessel and valet Peter Quint are possessing the children. Miss Giddens decides to help the children to face and exorcise the spirits.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 21st October</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627617\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">1:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617472/halloween-ii-1981\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/P3QfPFEHstMmKpVHnx0CdbGQmBFKFjb-BtWF_IxWuXk.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617472/halloween-ii-1981\" target=\"\">Halloween II (1981)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>92mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Rick Rosenthal</span>                                        <span>Starring Jamie Lee Curtis, Donald Pleasence, Charles Cyphers, The Shape</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>After failing to kill stubborn survivor Laurie and taking a bullet or six from former psychiatrist Dr. Sam Loomis, Michael Myers has followed Laurie to the Haddonfield Memorial Hospital, where she's been admitted for Myers' attempt on her life. The institution proves to be particularly suited to serial killers, however, as Myers cuts, stabs and slashes his way through hospital staff to reach his favorite victim.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 21st October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627614\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row live-score\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616917/haxan\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31616917.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616917/haxan\" target=\"\">Haxan</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1922</span>                                        <span>106mins</span>                                                                                <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Benjamin Christensen</span>                                        <span>Starring Benjamin Christensen, Ella La Cour, Emmy Schønfeld</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>This performance will feature a live score performed by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/hugo_max_scores_silents/\">Hugo Max</a></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Benjamin Christensen&rsquo;s&nbsp;<strong>H&auml;xan</strong>&nbsp;must to be seen to be believed. Playing out as a lecture on witchcraft &lsquo;made flesh&rsquo;, the film foreshadows the found footage horror genre and features many of the most imaginatively realised and grotesque visuals of silent cinema history. My viola takes on the voice of the occult-obsessed lecturer(/director), possessed by the alluring darkness of the subject, wrestling with the film&rsquo;s message of hierarchal corruption and its prevailing controversies</em>.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlease view <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z7rvOLnMpGM\">this&nbsp;YouTube video</a>&nbsp;for a sample of Hugo&#39;s work.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 22nd October</div>                                                <li class=\"live-score\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626005\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag live-score\">LIVE SCORE</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617461/cube\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/u3FBdq3jMTSGCD6iS1mhNePNHob0np8B5lQPxspCpz0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617461/cube\" target=\"\">Cube</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1997</span>                                        <span>90mins</span>                                        <span>Canada</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Mystery</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Vincenzo Natali</span>                                        <span>Starring Nicole De Boer, Nicky Guadagni, Maurice Dean Wint</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A group of strangers find themselves trapped in a maze-like prison. It soon becomes clear that each of them possesses the peculiar skills necessary to escape, if they don't wind up dead first.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 22nd October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627512\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11246659/solve-along-a-murder-she-wrote\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/11246659.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11246659/solve-along-a-murder-she-wrote\" target=\"\">Solve Along A Murder She Wrote</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1984</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>PCC Event</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by  Various</span>                                        <span>Starring Angela Lansbury</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Cult hit event Solve-Along-A-Murder-She-Wrote returns to the Prince Charles Cinema with an interactive screening of a classic Murder, She Wrote episode. Watch as Cabot Cove gets caught up in a murder mystery only JB Fletcher (or you!) can solve!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSolve-Along-A-Murder-She-Wrote is a unique and hilarious night featuring games, prizes and audience participation, with special permission from NBC Universal Television. See the show Time Out rated one of 2021 and 2019&rsquo;s 50 Great Nights Out in London that has played to sell-out audiences across the UK and Australia.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nHosted by super-fan Tim Benzie, Solve-Along-A-Murder-She-Wrote features:<br />\r\n* A race to solve to the crime, via the Fameometer and the Suspiciometer!<br />\r\n* A Cabot Cove quiz!<br />\r\n* A singalong to the theme tune with new lyrics!<br />\r\n* Clips and biogs of the campy guest stars!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTim Benzie is obsessed with Murder, She Wrote, having watched the original series when it was first broadcast, and now relishing the repeats on television everywhere. Tim is the writer/performer of &ldquo;It&rsquo;s a Mystery!&rdquo;, all about our love of whodunnits. An award-winning playwright and co-writer of the Royal Vauxhall Tavern&rsquo;s 2017-2023 pantos (&lsquo;Goosed&rsquo;, &lsquo;Rubbed&rsquo;, &lsquo;Slipped&rsquo;, &lsquo;Pricked&rsquo;, &lsquo;Cracked&rsquo; and &lsquo;Tossed&rsquo;). He is the co-producer of the camp club night PopHorror.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nVisit us at&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.solvealongamurdershewrote.com/\">www.solvealongamurdershewrote.com</a>, or follow us on Instagram, Twitter and Facebook @solvealonga.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>2026 SCHEDULE:</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Tuesday 8th September 2026</strong><br />\r\n&quot;Dead Man&#39;s Gold&quot;&nbsp;<br />\r\nDirected by Seymour Robbie<br />\r\nStarring Angela Lansbury, Leslie Nielsen, Tom Bosley<br />\r\n1986 | 120mins | USA</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Thursday 22nd October 2026</strong><br />\r\nEncore Halloween special - &quot;The Witch&#39;s Curse&quot;<br />\r\nDirected by Jerry Jameson<br />\r\nStarring Angela Lansbury, Robert Vaughn, Mary Crosby<br />\r\n1992 | 120mins | USA</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Thursday 26th November 2026</strong><br />\r\nNew episode TBC</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Thursday 17th December 2026</strong><br />\r\nEncore screening - &quot;A Christmas Secret&quot;<br />\r\nDirected by Anthony Pullen Shaw<br />\r\nStarring Angela Lansbury, Larry Wilcox, Amy Brenneman<br />\r\n1992 | 120mins | USA<br />\r\n<br />\r\n***<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>The Critics speak!</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;You&rsquo;ll be swept away with Jessica Fletcher feels &hellip; it has the BEST HOST.&rdquo; - Time Out London<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&quot;A cinematic, theatrical and hilarious experience&nbsp;... Before the night I had never seen an episode of Murder, She Wrote before, unlike some dedicated fans who had even dressed up. However, this really was an evening everyone could enjoy.&rdquo; - Nottingham Post <br />\r\n<br />\r\n&quot;As soon as I saw it was on at the [Edinburgh] Fringe I elbowed my way through the other BW reviewers, pushed a couple of them over &hellip; just so I could get to the front of the queue and see this show again. And&nbsp;it did not disappoint ... I&#39;d go again in a heartbeat.&rdquo; 5 stars ***** - Broadway World<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&quot;The self-confessed super-fan and award-winning playwright will lead you into&nbsp;a silly whirlwind of nostalgic giggle, using his wealth of camp trivia and sound logic to solve these killings.&rdquo; 5 stars ***** - One4Review<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&quot;Benzie knows how to put on a great show ...&nbsp;I would happily see it again, with all the fervour of the &lsquo;Jessica Fletcher eating popcorn&rsquo; meme.&quot; 5 stars ***** - Everything Theatre<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;Whodunnit? Tim dunnit &ndash; and he did it so well I can&rsquo;t wait for the next one!&quot; 5 stars ***** - Fairy-Powered Productions<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;I&rsquo;d challenge anyone to sit through this show and not get utterly invested in figuring out whodunit.&rdquo; 4 stars **** - West End Wilma<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;This is a highly entertaining production even if you have never seen an episode, filled with outrageous fun.&quot; 4 stars **** - British Theatre Guide<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&quot;For a funny, campy evening, there is little that could beat Solve-Along-A-Murder-She-Wrote&rsquo;s unique qualities and Benzie&rsquo;s wit and charm. Personally this reviewer can&rsquo;t wait to revisit  Cabot Cove. Never mind &#39;whodunnit&#39;, more like &#39;yougottadoit!&quot; 4 stars **** - The Reviews Hub<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;A lighthearted two hours of entertainment that both die-hard devotees and Cabot Cove novices will enjoy ...&nbsp;A solve-along,&nbsp;sing-along hit.&quot; 4 stars **** - Broadway Baby<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;Benzie&#39;s passion and knowledge shines through.&quot; 4 stars **** - West End Best Friend<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&quot;Tim Benzie is the perfect host ...&nbsp;Benzie&rsquo;s insights help keep the audience engaged with the show and not just passively watching the episode unfold.&rdquo; 4 stars **** - The Nerd Party<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;It didn&rsquo;t take long for Benzie to have the audience in stitches and he had the whole crowd in the palm of his hand the entire evening.&rdquo; - Bristol 24/7<br />\r\n<br />\r\n&ldquo;A unique and thoroughly enjoyable theatre experience&rdquo; - Blue Curtains Brisbane<br />\r\n<br />\r\n***<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFor links to the full reviews visit&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.solvealongamurdershewrote.com/\">www.solvealongamurdershewrote.com</a><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" height=\"360\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/643021192?h=29f9d6b516\" title=\"vimeo-player\" width=\"640\"></iframe></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 22nd October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627228\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627229\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 17th December</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627230\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617473/rob-zombies-halloween-2007\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/3Rf1YDTWhRvetcuUhjnhBHkt2MTLZSXvzMKHflmIwTU.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617473/rob-zombies-halloween-2007\" target=\"\">Rob Zombie&#039;s Halloween (2007)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2007</span>                                        <span>110mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Rob Zombie</span>                                        <span>Starring Scout Taylor-Compton, Malcolm McDowell, Tyler Mane, Danielle Harris</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>After being committed for 15 years, Michael Myers, now a grown man and still very dangerous, escapes from the mental institution and immediately returns to Haddonfield to find his baby sister, Laurie.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 23rd October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627622\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617474/rob-zombies-halloween-ii-2009\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/rBmd_cjvsNDT3eEvv2HO7zzP2y5_PNDG7jOgmTPCE4w.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617474/rob-zombies-halloween-ii-2009\" target=\"\">Rob Zombie&#039;s Halloween II (2009)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2009</span>                                        <span>105mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Rob Zombie</span>                                        <span>Starring Scout Taylor-Compton, Malcolm McDowell, Tyler Mane</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Laurie Strode struggles to come to terms with her brother Michael's deadly return to Haddonfield, Illinois; meanwhile, Michael prepares for another reunion with his sister.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 23rd October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627628\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/25245690/scoobydooble-feature\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/25245690.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/25245690/scoobydooble-feature\" target=\"\">Scooby-Dooble Feature</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2002</span>                                        <span>198mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Movie Marathons</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Raja Gosnell</span>                                        <span>Starring Freddie Prinze Jr, Freddie Prinze Jr., Linda Cardellini, Matthew Lillard, Rowan Atkinson, Sarah Michelle Gellar</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><em>Don&#39;t miss the return of the original <strong>SCOOBY-DOOBLE FEATURE</strong> : featuring the loveable 2002 live-action adaptation of the classic Hanna-Barbera cartoon series, <strong>SCOOBY-DOO</strong>, and its 2004 sequel,<strong> SCOOBY DOO 2: MONSTERS UNLEASHED</strong>, back-to-back from 35mm prints in one night! Accept no imitations!</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>SCOOBY-DOO (2002) : Zoinks! Two years after a clash of egos forced Mystery Inc. to close its doors, Scooby-Doo and his clever crime-solving cohorts Fred (Freddie Prinze Jr.), Daphne (Sarah Michelle Gellar), Shaggy (Matthew Lillard) and Velma (Linda Cardellini) are individually summoned to Spooky Island to investigate a series of paranormal incidents at the ultra-hip Spring Break hot spot.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nSCOOBY-DOO 2: MONSTERS UNLEASHED (2004) : In this live-action sequel, the lovable dog Scooby-Doo once again joins his pals Shaggy (Matthew Lillard), Velma (Linda Cardellini), Fred (Freddie Prinze Jr.) and Daphne (Sarah Michelle Gellar) as they stumble into another seemingly supernatural mystery. In addition to facing off against various monsters that are tormenting their town, the gang must deal with television journalist Heather Jasper-Howe (Alicia Silverstone), who is out to discredit their investigations.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 23rd October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627630\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616717/were-all-going-to-the-worlds-fair\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/fXn4Nz1WCTEmzAFvwgEZoPHvptR.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616717/were-all-going-to-the-worlds-fair\" target=\"\">We&#039;re All Going to the World&#039;s Fair</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2021</span>                                        <span>86mins</span>                                                                                <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jane Schoenbrun</span>                                        <span>Starring Anna Cobb, Michael J Rogers, May Leitz</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Reality and fantasy begin to blur when a teenager, alone in her attic bedroom, immerses herself in a role-playing horror game online.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 24th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627639\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616715/i-saw-the-tv-glow\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31616715.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616715/i-saw-the-tv-glow\" target=\"\">I Saw the TV Glow</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2024</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jane Schoenbrun</span>                                        <span>Starring Justice Smith, Jack Haven, Ian Foreman</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Teenager Owen is just trying to make it through life in the suburbs when his classmate introduces him to a mysterious late-night TV show &mdash; a vision of a supernatural world beneath their own. In the pale glow of the television, Owen&rsquo;s view of reality begins to crack.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 24th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627640\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617418/teenage-sex-and-death-at-camp-miasma\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/Lu6AldvHCdcWn79H8ElFL9uYMOdGsZwHXQ0Mes3hvPo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617418/teenage-sex-and-death-at-camp-miasma\" target=\"\">Teenage Sex and Death at Camp Miasma</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>112mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jane Schoenbrun</span>                                        <span>Starring Hannah Einbinder, Gillian Anderson, Amanda Fix</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Hacks breakout star Hannah Einbinder and, in a playful bit of meta-casting, Gillian Anderson (The X Files, Sex Education) headline this heady, gory slasher homage from writer-director Jane Schoenbrun. Like Schoenbrun&rsquo;s previous films I Saw the TV Glow and We&rsquo;re All Going to the World&rsquo;s Fair, it uses a horror genre lens to explore a rich array of themes and ideas &ndash; queer identity and sexuality, memory and nostalgia, the nature of female desire, the state of the entertainment industry &ndash; with humour, vulnerability and affection.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After years of slapdash sequels, the Camp Miasma slasher franchise is handed over to an enthusiastic, cerebral young director (Einbinder) &ndash; who credits the first film with her own queer awakening &ndash; to resurrect. But fantasy and reality collide when she visits the original film&rsquo;s star (Anderson), now a mysterious recluse living on its old set, and the two women fall into a blood-soaked world of fear, desire and delirium</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 24th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627641\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617175/mystery-horror-movie-marathon\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31617175.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617175/mystery-horror-movie-marathon\" target=\"\">Mystery Horror Movie Marathon</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1896</span>                                        <span>500mins</span>                                        <span>We can't tell you</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Movie Marathons</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Who Knows?</span>                                        <span>Starring  Various</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/AllNighterRules.pdf\"><strong>ALL NIGHTER : FAQs, HOUSE RULES &amp; TIPS</strong></a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong><em>Please Note: We will have a late licence on the night, and the bar will close at 2am.</em></strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\nDon&#39;t miss a &nbsp;MYSTERY HORROR MOVIE MARATHON,&nbsp;featuring 5 random horror films that have been plucked from the history of the genre!&nbsp;No Clues! No Hints! No Refunds! Only Dread!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTickets are only &pound;20 Non-Members / &pound;17.50 Members!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThat&#39;s an incredible deal for 5 films; so why not take a chance and let a little mystery into your life!?!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nMYSTERY HORROR MOVIE MARATHON&nbsp;line-up<br />\r\n&bull; MYSTERY MOVIE 1<br />\r\n&bull; MYSTERY MOVIE 2<br />\r\n&bull; MYSTERY MOVIE 3<br />\r\n&bull; MYSTERY MOVIE 4<br />\r\n&bull; MYSTERY MOVIE 5<br />\r\n<br />\r\n(We will update end time shortly)<br />\r\n<br />\r\n------------------------<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNO ADMISSIONS TO THE CINEMA AFTER MIDNIGHT<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNO ALCOHOL PURCHASED FROM OUTSIDE IS PERMITTED IN THE BUILDING!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAGE RESTRICTIONS: This event is strictly 18+</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 24th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627841\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm-dcp\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616767/classic-horror-marathon\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/EyhPsQ-HuLRKRRNAMfYKRpfDe5oA_wAYlx0owmwAz2k.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616767/classic-horror-marathon\" target=\"\">Classic Horror Marathon</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1974</span>                                        <span>533mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Movie Marathons</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Carpenter|William Friedkin|Stanley Kubrick|Wes Craven|Tobe Hooper</span>                                        <span>Starring Kurt Russell, Ellen Burstyn, Jack Nicholson, Robert Englund, Marilyn Burns</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/AllNighterRules.pdf\"><strong>ALL NIGHTER : FAQs, HOUSE RULES &amp; TIPS</strong></a><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>THE THING :&nbsp;</strong>In remote Antarctica, a group of American research scientists are disturbed at their base camp by a helicopter shooting at a sled dog. When they take in the dog, it brutally attacks both human beings and canines in the camp and they discover that the beast can assume the shape of its victims. A resourceful helicopter pilot (Kurt Russell) and the camp doctor (Richard Dysart) lead the camp crew in a desperate, gory battle against the vicious creature before it picks them all off, one by one.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>THE EXORCIST (Extended Cut)&nbsp;:&nbsp;</strong>When young Regan (Linda Blair) starts acting odd -- levitating, speaking in tongues -- her worried mother (Ellen Burstyn) seeks medical help, only to hit a dead end. A local priest (Jason Miller), however, thinks the girl may be seized by the devil. The priest makes a request to perform an exorcism, and the church sends in an expert (Max von Sydow) to help with the difficult job.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>THE SHINING&nbsp;:&nbsp;</strong>Jack Torrance (Jack Nicholson) becomes winter caretaker at the isolated Overlook Hotel in Colorado, hoping to cure his writer&#39;s block. He settles in along with his wife, Wendy (Shelley Duvall), and his son, Danny (Danny Lloyd), who is plagued by psychic premonitions. As Jack&#39;s writing goes nowhere and Danny&#39;s visions become more disturbing, Jack discovers the hotel&#39;s dark secrets and begins to unravel into a homicidal maniac hell-bent on terrorizing his family.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>A NIGHTMARE ON ELM STREET:&nbsp;</strong>In Wes Craven&#39;s classic slasher film, several Midwestern teenagers fall prey to Freddy Krueger (Robert Englund), a disfigured midnight mangler who preys on the teenagers in their dreams -- which, in turn, kills them in reality. After investigating the phenomenon, Nancy (Heather Langenkamp) begins to suspect that a dark secret kept by her and her friends&#39; parents may be the key to unraveling the mystery, but can Nancy and her boyfriend Glen (Johnny Depp) solve the puzzle before it&#39;s too late?<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>THE TEXAS CHAIN SAW MASSACRE&nbsp;:&nbsp;</strong>When Sally (Marilyn Burns) hears that her grandfather&#39;s grave may have been vandalized, she and her paraplegic brother, Franklin (Paul A. Partain), set out with their friends to investigate. After a detour to their family&#39;s old farmhouse, they discover a group of crazed, murderous outcasts living next door. As the group is attacked one by one by the chainsaw-wielding Leatherface (Gunnar Hansen), who wears a mask of human skin, the survivors must do everything they can to escape.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Marathon is due to end at 08:38am</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>Please Note: The Bar closes at 11pm</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\n-------------------------<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>NO ADMISSIONS TO THE CINEMA AFTER MIDNIGHT!</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>NO ALCOHOL PURCHASED FROM OUTSIDE IS PERMITTED IN THE BUILDING!</em><br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>AGE RESTRICTIONS: This event is strictly 18+</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 24th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm-dcp\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627840\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm-dcp\">35mm / DCP</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23839276/night-of-the-living-dead-1968\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/23839276.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23839276/night-of-the-living-dead-1968\" target=\"\">Night of the Living Dead (1968)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1968</span>                                        <span>96mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by George A. Romero</span>                                        <span>Starring Duane Jones, Judith O'Dea, Karl Hardman</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>New 4K Restoration!</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>A disparate group of individuals takes refuge in an abandoned house when corpses begin to leave the graveyard in search of fresh human bodies to devour. The pragmatic Ben (Duane Jones) does his best to control the situation, but when the re-animated bodies surround the house, the other survivors begin to panic. As any semblance of order within the group begins to dissipate, the zombies start to find ways inside. One by one, the living humans become the prey of the deceased ones.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><em>&quot;Night of the Living Dead was restored by the Museum of Modern Art and The Film Foundation, with funding provided by the George Lucas Family Foundation and the Celeste Bartos Preservation Fund.&quot;</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 25th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627648\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">1:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11427203/shaun-of-the-dead\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/zjj-ENUfLsSMmZmOwSXzmh6tgDqY9LjEcy9oxmh-A18.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11427203/shaun-of-the-dead\" target=\"\">Shaun of the Dead</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2004</span>                                        <span>99mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Edgar Wright</span>                                        <span>Starring Simon Pegg, Nick Frost, Kate Ashfield, Lucy Davis, Dylan Moran, Peter Serafinowicz</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>There comes a day in every man's life when he has to get off the couch…and kill some zombies. When flesh-eating zombies are on the hunt for a bite to eat, it's up to slacker Shaun and his best pal to save their friends and family from becoming the next entrée.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 25th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627788\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3436/the-return-of-the-living-dead\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3436.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3436/the-return-of-the-living-dead\" target=\"\">The Return of the Living Dead</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1985</span>                                        <span>91mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Dan O'Bannon</span>                                        <span>Starring Clu Gulager, Don Calfa, James Karen</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When foreman Frank (James Karen) shows new employee Freddy (Thom Mathews) a secret military experiment in a supply warehouse, the two klutzes accidentally release a gas that reanimates corpses into flesh-eating zombies. As the epidemic spreads throughout Louisville, Ky., and the creatures satisfy their hunger in gory and outlandish ways, Frank and Freddy fight to survive with the help of their boss (Clu Gulager) and a mysterious mortician (Don Calfa).</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 25th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627646\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616661/the-cable-guy\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31616661.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616661/the-cable-guy\" target=\"\">The Cable Guy</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>96mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Ben Stiller</span>                                        <span>Starring Jack Black, Jim Carrey, Matthew Broderick, Leslie Mann</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>* ON SALE 23rd SEP *</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Oddball cable installer Chip Douglas (Jim Carrey) attempts to strike up a friendship with customer Steven Kovacs (Matthew Broderick) by offering him premium channels at no cost. When Steven rebuffs Chip&#39;s frequent need for companionship, Chip goes from a mildly eccentric acquaintance to a full-fledged psycho stalker. Though it&#39;s increasingly apparent to Steven that the cable guy is dangerous, convincing his friends, family and the authorities of that is another matter entirely.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 26th October</div>                                                <li class=\"1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627653\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/618627/friday-the-13th\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/618627.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/618627/friday-the-13th\" target=\"\">Friday The 13th</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1980</span>                                        <span>95mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Sean S. Cunningham</span>                                        <span>Starring Betsy Palmer, Adrienne King, Jeannine Taylor</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A group of teenage camp counselors attempt to re-open an abandoned summer camp with a tragic past, but they are stalked by a mysterious, relentless killer.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 27th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627661\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 31st October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627691\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616848/prince-charles-cinema-film-quiz\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/ou9HwNBzccunTiXhHVQZ2PPA13zSsXWrhPwj-hvrulw.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616848/prince-charles-cinema-film-quiz\" target=\"\">Prince Charles Cinema Film Quiz</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2024</span>                                        <span>140mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Film Quiz</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Chevy Mclaren</span>                                                                            </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\"><em><strong>Put your cinematic knowledge to the test with The Prince Charles Cinema Film Quiz!</strong></em></span><br />\r\n<br />\r\nThis is a&nbsp;full-blown, no-holds-barred celebration of cinematic chaos, cult classics, and endless movie trivia. Hosted by Chevy Mclaren live in the&nbsp;heart of London cinema -&nbsp;this is your chance to test your film knowledge in this night of movie madness!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Expect limited-edition PCC merch, free cinema tickets, exclusive movie prizes, live performances, and bonkers audience games. Bring your cinephile friends (teams up to 5), grab a drink, and prepare to scream, guess, act, and laugh your way through the most chaotic&nbsp;quiz night in London!</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 27th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627852\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 1st December</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627888\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617475/3-from-hell\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/DLIQl9mTR5DBttrfg-1hwFIznA5uqPLz8umBeDrtPDA.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617475/3-from-hell\" target=\"\">3 from Hell</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2019</span>                                        <span>115mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Rob Zombie</span>                                        <span>Starring Sheri Moon Zombie, Bill Moseley, Richard Brake</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>After barely surviving a furious shootout with the police, Baby Firefly, Otis Driftwood and Captain Spaulding are behind bars. But pure evil cannot be contained. Teaming up with Otis' half-brother Winslow, the demented Firefly clan escape to unleash a whole new wave of murder, madness and mayhem.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 28th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627671\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617050/brother\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/Gsh8eFnlhyhJ7iyp94AgvPGol67XDcNXrQp-5LhKxKU.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617050/brother\" target=\"\">Brother</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2000</span>                                        <span>114mins</span>                                        <span>France, Japan, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Takeshi Kitano</span>                                        <span>Starring Takeshi Kitano, Omar Epps, Claude Maki</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Legendary comedian and TV host turned director Takeshi Kitano writes, directs, and stars in his first and only American co-production. Disgraced yakuza Yamamoto (Kitano) seeks refuge in Los Angeles, reconnecting with his younger half-brother Ken (Claude Maki) after his clan suffered defeat at the hands of a rival gang back in Tokyo. Cool and detached, Brother marries Japanese and American disillusionment in Kitano&rsquo;s signature violent minimalist style through the growing bonds between Yamamoto and the multinational gang that he cultivates in L.A.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><em><strong>Brother is featured as part of Gangsters Have Feelings Too, a season exploring the sensitive gangster film. The season is presented with the National Film and Television School&rsquo;s Film Studies, Programming and Curation MA.</strong></em></span></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 28th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627670\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1257190/interview-with-the-vampire\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1257190.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1257190/interview-with-the-vampire\" target=\"\">Interview With The Vampire</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1994</span>                                        <span>122mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Neil Jordan</span>                                        <span>Starring Tom Cruise, Brad Pitt, Antonio Banderas</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Born as an 18th-century lord, Louis is now a bicentennial vampire, telling his story to an eager biographer. Suicidal after the death of his family, he meets Lestat, a vampire who persuades him to choose immortality over death and become his companion. Eventually, gentle Louis resolves to leave his violent maker, but Lestat guilts him into staying by turning a young girl -- whose addition to the \"family\" breeds even more conflict.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 29th October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628243\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3289/from-dusk-till-dawn\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/S2P-wwOMcql8mwRzcpQZoy_ekzjbddb76eaOAlYFRwM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3289/from-dusk-till-dawn\" target=\"\">From Dusk Till Dawn</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>108mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Action</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Robert Rodriguez</span>                                        <span>Starring George Clooney, Harvey Keitel, Juliette Lewis, Quentin Tarantino, Selma Hayek</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>After kidnapping a father and his two kids, the Gecko brothers head south to a seedy Mexican bar to hide out in safety, unaware of its notorious clientele.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 29th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627674\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3221048/bram-stokers-dracula\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3221048.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3221048/bram-stokers-dracula\" target=\"\">Bram Stoker&#039;s Dracula</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1992</span>                                        <span>127mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Francis Ford Coppola</span>                                        <span>Starring Anthony Hopkins, Gary Oldman, Winona Ryder</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Count Dracula, a 15th-century prince, is condemned to live off the blood of the living for eternity. Young lawyer Jonathan Harker is sent to Dracula's castle to finalise a land deal, but when the Count sees a photo of Harker's fiancée, Mina, the spitting image of his dead wife, he imprisons him and sets off for London to track her down.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 29th October</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627673\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19477989/blade\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/19477989.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19477989/blade\" target=\"\">Blade</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1998</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Supernatural / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Stephen Norrington</span>                                        <span>Starring Stephen Dorff, Wesley Snipes, Kris Kristofferson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A half-mortal, half-immortal is out to avenge his mother's death and rid the world of vampires. The modern-day technologically advanced vampires he is going after are in search of his special blood type needed to summon an evil god who plays a key role in their plan to execute the human race.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 29th October</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627675\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617462/halloween-marathon\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/63MCbRbkoEtQN4fpgOM_p8jGgP3qVvpYqTaxg75iUNs.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617462/halloween-marathon\" target=\"\">Halloween Marathon</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1978</span>                                        <span>617mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Movie Marathons</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Carpenter| Various</span>                                        <span>Starring Jamie Lee Curtis, Donald Pleasence, The Shape, Danielle Harris, Paul Rudd</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/AllNighterRules.pdf\"><strong>ALL NIGHTER : FAQs, HOUSE RULES &amp; TIPS</strong></a><br />\r\n<br />\r\nHALLOWEEN (1978):&nbsp;Fifteen years after murdering his sister on Halloween Night 1963, Michael Myers escapes from a mental hospital and returns to the small town of Haddonfield, Illinois to kill again.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>HALLOWEEN II (1981):&nbsp;After failing to kill stubborn survivor Laurie and taking a bullet or six from former psychiatrist Dr. Sam Loomis, Michael Myers has followed Laurie to the Haddonfield Memorial Hospital, where she&rsquo;s been admitted for Myers&rsquo; attempt on her life. The institution proves to be particularly suited to serial killers, however, as Myers cuts, stabs and slashes his way through hospital staff to reach his favourite victim.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>HALLOWEEN III: SEASON OF THE WITCH (1982):&nbsp;After a terrified toy salesman is mysteriously attacked and brought to the hospital, clutching the year&rsquo;s most popular Halloween mask, Dr. Daniel Challis sets out to investigate the strange events and finds himself thrust into a nightmarish conspiracy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>HALLOWEEN 4: THE RETURN OF MICHAEL MYERS (1988):&nbsp;Ten years after his original massacre, the invalid Michael Myers awakens on Halloween Eve and returns to Haddonfield to kill his seven-year-old niece.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>HALLOWEEN 5: THE REVENGE OF MICHAEL MYERS (1989):&nbsp;After lying in a coma for a year, Michael Myers awakens and stalks his way back to his small hometown in Illinois, intent on killing his niece, Jamie, who has been confined to a mental institution since his last attempt to slay her.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>HALLOWEEN: THE CURSE OF MICHAEL MYERS [Producer&#39;s Cut]&nbsp;(1995):&nbsp;Six years after being presumed dead in a fire, and just as the town prepares to finally celebrate Halloween again, Michael Myers returns to Haddonfield to continue his reign of terror.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNO ADMISSIONS TO THE CINEMA AFTER MIDNIGHT<br />\r\n<br />\r\nNO ALCOHOL PURCHASED FROM OUTSIDE IS PERMITTED IN THE BUILDING!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAGE RESTRICTIONS: This event is strictly 18+</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 31st October</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627796\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627518\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3639584/donnie-darko-theatrical-cut\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3639584.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3639584/donnie-darko-theatrical-cut\" target=\"\">Donnie Darko [Theatrical Cut]</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2001</span>                                        <span>113mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Science Fiction</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Richard Kelly</span>                                        <span>Starring Jake Gyllenhaal, Jena Malone, Mary McDonnell</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>During the presidential election of 1988, a teenager named Donnie Darko sleepwalks out of his house one night and sees a giant, demonic-looking rabbit named Frank, who tells him the world will end in 28 days. When Donnie returns home, he finds that a jet engine has crashed into his bedroom. Is Donnie living in a parallel universe, is he suffering from mental illness - or will the world really end?</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 1st November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627699\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/25079278/in-the-realm-of-the-sense\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/9OS4JWD9E7VVIDXg00cEJUmOhN6GUqN4vuJJSmLRmaA.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/25079278/in-the-realm-of-the-sense\" target=\"\">In the Realm of the Sense</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1976</span>                                        <span>102mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Psychological Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Nagisa Oshima</span>                                        <span>Starring Eiko Matsuda, Tatsuya Fuji, Aoi Nakajima, Taiji Tonoyama</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Still censored in its own country, In the Realm of the Senses (Ai no corrida), by Japanese director Nagisa Oshima, remains one of the most controversial films of all time. A graphic portrayal of insatiable sexual desire, Oshima&rsquo;s film, set in 1936 and based on a true incident, depicts a man and a woman (Tatsuya Fuji and Eiko Matsuda) consumed by a transcendent, destructive love while living in an era of ever-escalating imperialism and governmental control. Less a work of pornography than of politics, In the Realm of the Senses is a brave, taboo-breaking milestone.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Content Warning:&nbsp;This film contains scenes of graphic sex and violence. Further information about content and age-appropriateness for specific films can be found on <a href=\"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/\"><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\">Common Sense Media</span></a>, <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/\"><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\">IMDb</span></a> and <a href=\"https://www.doesthedogdie.com/\"><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\">DoesTheDogDie.com</span></a>, as well as through general internet searches.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 2nd November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628218\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 10th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628219\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/14138710/eyes-wide-shut\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/14138710.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/14138710/eyes-wide-shut\" target=\"\">Eyes Wide Shut</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1999</span>                                        <span>159mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Thriller / Mystery</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Stanley Kubrick</span>                                        <span>Starring Todd Field, Tom Cruise, Nicole Kidman, Sydney Pollack</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Stanley Kubrick&#39;s daring last film is many things. It is a compelling psychosexual journey. A haunting dreamscape. A riveting tale of suspense. A major milestone in the careers of stars Tom Cruise and Nicole Kidman. And &quot;a worthy final chapter to a great director&#39;s career&quot; (Roger Ebert).<br />\r\n<br />\r\nCruise plays Dr William Hartford, who plunges into an erotic foray that threatens his marriage - and may even ensnare him in a lurid murder mystery - after his wife&#39;s (Kidman) admission of sexual longings. As the story sweeps from doubt and fear to self-discovery and reconciliation, Kubrick orchestrates it with masterful flourishes. Graceful tracking shots, controlled pacing, rich colours, startling images: bravura traits that make Kubrick a filmmaker for the ages are here to keep everyone&#39;s eyes wide shut.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 2nd November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628217\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 27th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627858\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 4th December</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628030\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Monday 7th December</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628044\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 15th December</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628119\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 16th December</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628128\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617528/arsenic-and-old-lace\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/6x5ZqH4WhLxLdmXO2KYlaQm6j5swp1xHTJeKIxLCmiA.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617528/arsenic-and-old-lace\" target=\"\">Arsenic and Old Lace</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1944</span>                                        <span>118mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Comedy/Crime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Frank Capra</span>                                        <span>Starring Cary Grant, Priscilla Lane, Josephine Hull</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>*ON SALE 23rd OCT *\r\n\r\nMortimer Brewster, a newspaper drama critic, playwright, and author known for his diatribes against marriage, suddenly falls in love and gets married;  but when he makes a quick trip home to tell his two maiden aunts, he finds out his aunts' hobby - killing lonely old men and burying them in the cellar!</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 2nd November</div>                                                <li class=\"1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628221\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11808120/antichrist\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/11808120.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11808120/antichrist\" target=\"\">Antichrist</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2009</span>                                        <span>108mins</span>                                        <span>Denmark, France, Germany, Italy, Poland, Sweden</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Mystery</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Lars von Trier</span>                                        <span>Starring Charlotte Gainsbourg, Storm Acheche Sahlstrøm, Willem Dafoe</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>While a married couple (Willem Dafoe, Charlotte Gainsbourg) is having sex, their infant son in a nearby room falls out a window to his death. She becomes distraught and is hospitalized, but her husband, who is a psychiatrist, attempts to treat her. Deciding that she needs to face her fears, he takes her to a cabin in the woods where she spent a previous summer with the boy. Once they are there, she becomes more unhinged and starts perpetrating sexual violence on her husband and herself.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 3rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628225\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/189195/black-narcissus\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/Qf6iptYxS29QRlpeeHschy6jLfp2CJJjwxdneLnICQA.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/189195/black-narcissus\" target=\"\">Black Narcissus</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1947</span>                                        <span>101mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Psychological Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Michael Powell|Emeric Pressburger</span>                                        <span>Starring Deborah Kerr, Kathleen Byron, Flora Robson, David Farrar</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>This explosive work about the conflict between the spirit and the flesh is the epitome of the sensuous style of Michael Powell and Emeric Pressburger. A group of nuns—played by some of Britain's finest actresses, including Deborah Kerr, Kathleen Byron, and Flora Robson—struggle to establish a convent in the Himalayas, while isolation, extreme weather, altitude, and culture clashes all conspire to drive the well-intentioned missionaries mad. A darkly grand film that won Oscars for Alfred Junge's art direction and Jack Cardiff's cinematography, Black Narcissus is one of the greatest achievements by two of cinema's true visionaries.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 3rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628224\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/30030716/the-zone-of-interest\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/t9ebSPa_oVjKqEHYSQC13FpsIN6tD1e2LarGlUyKl0Y.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/30030716/the-zone-of-interest\" target=\"\">The Zone of Interest</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2023</span>                                        <span>105mins</span>                                        <span>Poland, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Psychological Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jonathan Glazer</span>                                        <span>Starring Sandra Hüller, Christian Friedel</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>The commandant of Auschwitz, Rudolf Höss, and his wife Hedwig, strive to build a dream life for their family in a house and garden next to the camp.The commandant of Auschwitz, Rudolf Höss, and his wife Hedwig, strive to build a dream life for their family in a house and garden next to the camp.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 3rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627510\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1787253/la-la-land\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1787253.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1787253/la-la-land\" target=\"\">La La Land</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2016</span>                                        <span>128mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Musical</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Damien Chazelle</span>                                        <span>Starring Emma Stone, Ryan Gosling, Rosemarie DeWitt</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Sebastian (Ryan Gosling) and Mia (Emma Stone) are drawn together by their common desire to do what they love. But as success mounts they are faced with decisions that begin to fray the fragile fabric of their love affair, and the dreams they worked so hard to maintain in each other threaten to rip them apart.<br /><br /></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 4th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628229\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627918\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/10519845/dogtooth-kynodontas\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/_M55iuysnnIkqXibCYGtFEj2yruKdzooGGG0rXRymsI.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/10519845/dogtooth-kynodontas\" target=\"\">Dogtooth [Kynodontas]</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2009</span>                                        <span>97mins</span>                                        <span>Greece</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Psychological Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Yorgos Lanthimos</span>                                        <span>Starring Christos Stergioglou, Michele Valley, Angeliki Papoulia</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Newly restored in 4K, DOGTOOTH follows a controlling, manipulative father who locks his three adult children in a state of perpetual childhood by keeping them prisoner within the sprawling family compound.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 4th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628230\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617280/fantastic-planet\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/bWqhrJjkSmwUdy40y9grpYh2dWA_2hHeGp1JKsXnwAo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617280/fantastic-planet\" target=\"\">Fantastic Planet</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1973</span>                                        <span>72mins</span>                                        <span>Czechoslovakia, France</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Animation</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by René Laloux</span>                                        <span>Starring Gérard Hernandez, Jean Valmont, Jennifer Drake</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>On the planet Ygam, the Draags, extremely technologically and spiritually advanced blue humanoids, consider the tiny Oms, human beings descendants of Terra's inhabitants, as ignorant animals. Those who live in slavery are treated as simple pets and used to entertain Draag children; those who live hidden in the hostile wilderness of the planet are periodically hunted and ruthlessly slaughtered as if they were vermin.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 4th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627815\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616912/taste-of-cherry\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31616912.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616912/taste-of-cherry\" target=\"\">Taste of Cherry</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1997</span>                                        <span>99mins</span>                                        <span>Iran</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Abbas Kiarostami</span>                                        <span>Starring Homayoun Ershadi, Abdolrahman Bagheri, Safar Ali Moradi</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Winner of the Palme d&rsquo;Or at the 1997 Cannes Film Festival, Iranian auteur Abbas Kiarostami&rsquo;s _Taste of Cherry_ is an emotionally complex meditation on life and death. Middle-aged Mr. Badii (Homayoun Ershadi) drives through the hilly outskirts of Tehran&mdash;searching for someone to rescue or bury him.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 5th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628237\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 am</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/6052751/the-last-temptation-of-christ\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/hoE9c46Hv6R9bMXIXxv1l7Atc4GDGoe5V_4Ai6Tv0ME.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/6052751/the-last-temptation-of-christ\" target=\"\">The Last Temptation of Christ</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1988</span>                                        <span>164mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Martin Scorsese</span>                                        <span>Starring Willem Dafoe, Harvey Keitel, Barbara Hershey</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Jesus, a humble Judean carpenter beginning to see that he is the son of God, is drawn into revolutionary action against the Roman occupiers by Judas - despite his protestations that love, not violence, is the path to salvation. The burden of being the saviour of mankind torments Jesus throughout his life, leading him to doubt. As he is put to death on the cross, Jesus is tempted by visions of an ordinary life married to Mary Magdalene.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 5th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628238\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23054753/salo-or-the-120-days-of-sodom\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/23054753.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23054753/salo-or-the-120-days-of-sodom\" target=\"\">Salo, Or The 120 Days of Sodom</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1975</span>                                        <span>117mins</span>                                        <span>France, Italy</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Arthouse Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Pier Paolo Pasolini</span>                                        <span>Starring Paolo Bonacelli, Giorgio Cataldi, Uberto Paolo Quintavalle, Aldo Valletti, Caterina Boratto, Elsa De Giorgi</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Four corrupted fascist libertines round up 9 teenage boys and girls and subject them to 120 days of sadistic physical, mental and sexual&nbsp;torture.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 5th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628234\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:50 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9638984/twister\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/CTfSCEpx4HAd_BZsREjGoONlkIaWG6DkR1kNF-ATeIw.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9638984/twister\" target=\"\">Twister</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>113mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Action/Adventure</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jan de Bont</span>                                        <span>Starring Bill Paxton, Helen Hunt, Cary Elwes, Philip Seymour Hoffman</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Jo Harding (Helen Hunt) is a meteorologist on the brink of divorce from her husband, Bill (Bill Paxton). Before separating, they team up to develop a weather alert system by putting themselves in the path of violent tornadoes.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 5th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628235\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3273/v-for-vendetta\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3273.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3273/v-for-vendetta\" target=\"\">V For Vendetta</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2005</span>                                        <span>132mins</span>                                        <span>Germany, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi/Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by James McTeigue</span>                                        <span>Starring Hugo Weaving, Natalie Portman, Rupert Graves</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In a future British dystopian society, a shadowy freedom fighter, known only by the alias of \"V\", plots to overthrow the tyrannical government - with the help of a young woman.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 5th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628233\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:50 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/5909698/eternal-sunshine-of-the-spotless-mind\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/5909698.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/5909698/eternal-sunshine-of-the-spotless-mind\" target=\"\">Eternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mind</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2004</span>                                        <span>108mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Romance</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Michel Gondry</span>                                        <span>Starring Jim Carrey, Kate Winslet, Tom Wilkinson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>After a painful breakup, Clementine (Kate Winslet) undergoes a procedure to erase memories of her former boyfriend Joel (Jim Carrey) from her mind. When Joel discovers that Clementine is going to extremes to forget their relationship, he undergoes the same procedure and slowly begins to forget the woman that he loved. Directed by former music video director Michel Gondry, the visually arresting film explores the intricacy of relationships and the pain of loss.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 6th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628283\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 am</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617489/excalibur\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/Pxh1ArYfpiExkSLUHsiJbmPvgy6fsD9ddOBW2fqIDVI.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617489/excalibur\" target=\"\">Excalibur</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>141mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Adventure / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Boorman</span>                                        <span>Starring Nigel Terry, Nicol Williamson, Helen Mirren</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Arthur fulfills his fate by bringing together the Knights of the Round Table at Camelot and unifying the country. However, this flawed monarch faces greater tests ahead in pursuit of love, the Holy Grail, and his nation's survival.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 6th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627893\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4583163/short-cuts-35mm-roadshow-tour\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/RWeikBH5g_RIgNZMvKYbwLPLleFEyh1Bsd0Vpnxnfuk.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4583163/short-cuts-35mm-roadshow-tour\" target=\"\">Short Cuts : 35mm Roadshow Tour</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1993</span>                                        <span>188mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Robert Altman</span>                                        <span>Starring Tim Robbins, Julianne Moore, Andie MacDowell, Tom Waits</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>A multi-storied, fish-eyed look at the human condition against the backdrop of contemporary middle-class LA. Twenty two characters intersect, profoundly and fleetingly, through each other&rsquo;s lives. It runs the emotional gamut from disturbing to humorous.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<span style=\"color:#2ecc71\"><strong><em>Don&#39;t miss a rare opportunity to see&nbsp;Robert Altman&#39;s sprawling epic, showing from an original 35mm print as part of our SHORT CUTS 35mm Roadshow Tour. The 35mm Roadshow Tour will begin at the Prince Charles Cinema, before heading to other sites across the UK in a limited run this November. Special thanks to David Levy for helping us make this&nbsp;happen, and to Curzon for giving us and participating sites access to their print.</em></strong></span></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 6th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628284\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Monday 9th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628298\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 11th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628320\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3217862/bugsy-malone\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/_x4BkjJ95ks64M69ovBsZuHUHUca1cRf-4b9_SgjY4Q.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3217862/bugsy-malone\" target=\"\">Bugsy Malone</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1976</span>                                        <span>93mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Musical / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Alan Parker</span>                                        <span>Starring Jodie Foster, Scott Baio, Florrie Dugger</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>It is 1929 in New York and the city is divided by gang warfare. On one side, Dandy Dan's mob terrorise the district, taking out those they turn against with their new splurge guns. On the other side, Dandy Dan's rival, Fat Sam, runs his successful Grand Slam Speakeasy.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 7th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628288\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2631741/big-trouble-in-little-china\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/2631741.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2631741/big-trouble-in-little-china\" target=\"\">Big Trouble in Little China</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1986</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Action/Adventure</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Carpenter</span>                                        <span>Starring Dennis Dun, Kim Cattrall, Kurt Russell</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Kurt Russell plays hard-boiled truck driver Jack Burton, who gets caught in a bizarre conflict within, and underneath, San Francisco's Chinatown. An ancient Chinese prince and Chinatown crime lord has kidnapped a beautiful green-eyed woman, who is the fiancee to Jack's best friend. Jack must help his friend rescue the girl before the evil Lo Pan uses her to break the ancient curse that keeps him a fleshless and immortal spirit.<br /><br /></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 7th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628289\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 3rd December</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627958\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">1:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3475/romeo-juliet-1996\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3475.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3475/romeo-juliet-1996\" target=\"\">Romeo + Juliet (1996)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Romance</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Baz Luhrmann</span>                                        <span>Starring Leonardo DiCaprio, John Leguizamo, Claire Danes</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Against the urban backdrop of Verona Beach, California, the Montague and Capulet families are embroiled in a long-running feud. When Romeo, a Montague, attends a Capulet ball in disguise, he falls in love with the beautiful Juliet. Although already engaged to Dave Paris, whom she does not love, Juliet vows to marry Romeo. They ask the kindly Father Laurence to perform the ceremony in secret, but bloodshed and tragedy threaten the couple&#39;s future together.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 7th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628290\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k sub\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4534975/whisper-of-the-heart\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/868Zb_H4BL6tDXVJd3h0cveq-Rm1_N9PUiXxAlH_Ttc.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4534975/whisper-of-the-heart\" target=\"\">Whisper of the Heart</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1995</span>                                        <span>111mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Anime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Yoshifumi Kondô</span>                                        <span>Starring Yoko Honna, Issei Takahashi, Takashi Tachibana</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Discover the brilliance of this heartwarming coming-of-age classic from the legendary Studio Ghibli, creators of My Neighbour Totoro and the Academy Award&reg;-winning Spirited Away.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nA chance encounter with a mysterious cat sends Shizuku, a girl with her head in the clouds, on a quest for her true talent. Together with Seiji, a boy determined to follow his dreams, and enchanted by The Baron, an antique cat figurine who guides her to listen to the whispers of her heart, Shizuku embarks on a life-changing adventure that takes her beyond the boundaries of her imagination. Based on a screenplay and storyboards from Hayao Miyazaki, WHISPER OF THE HEART is a precious gem in the Studio Ghibli catalogue, directed by veteran animator Yoshifumi Kondo.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 8th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k sub\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628250\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span><span class=\"tag sub\">SUB</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 19th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k sub\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628251\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span><span class=\"tag sub\">SUB</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617490/the-7th-voyage-of-sinbad\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/1I4si3ehulLdtghriEdHWUZ4KmrPykGSrgHqVL9QMTI.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617490/the-7th-voyage-of-sinbad\" target=\"\">The 7th Voyage of Sinbad</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1958</span>                                        <span>88mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Adventure / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Nathan Juran</span>                                        <span>Starring Kerwin Mathews, Kathryn Grant, Torin Thatcher</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When a princess is shrunken by an evil wizard, Sinbad must undertake a quest to an island of monsters to cure her and prevent a war.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 8th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627894\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/8371373/pulp-fiction\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/8371373.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/8371373/pulp-fiction\" target=\"\">Pulp Fiction</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1994</span>                                        <span>155mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Quentin Tarantino</span>                                        <span>Starring John Travolta, Bruce Willis, Uma Thurman, Samuel L. Jackson, Ving Rhames</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Vincent Vega (John Travolta) and Jules Winnfield (Samuel L. Jackson) are hitmen with a penchant for philosophical discussions. In this ultra-hip, multi-strand crime movie, their storyline is interwoven with those of their boss, gangster Marsellus Wallace (Ving Rhames) ; his actress wife, Mia (Uma Thurman) ; struggling boxer Butch Coolidge (Bruce Willis) ; master fixer Winston Wolfe (Harvey Keitel) and a nervous pair of armed robbers, \"Pumpkin\" (Tim Roth) and \"Honey Bunny\" (Amanda Plummer).</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 9th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628297\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/12467699/oldboy-oldeuboi\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/12467699.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/12467699/oldboy-oldeuboi\" target=\"\">Oldboy [Oldeuboi]</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2003</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>South Korea</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Psychological Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Chan-wook Park</span>                                        <span>Starring Min-sik Choi, Ji-tae Yu, Hye-jeong Kang</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Dae-Su is an obnoxious drunk bailed from the police station yet again by a friend. However, he's abducted from the street and wakes up in a cell, where he remains for the next 15 years, drugged unconscious when human contact is unavoidable, otherwise with only the television as company. And then, suddenly released, he is invited to track down his jailor with a denouement that is simply stunning.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 9th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628301\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1480781/idiocracy\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1480781.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1480781/idiocracy\" target=\"\">Idiocracy</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2006</span>                                        <span>84mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Mike Judge</span>                                        <span>Starring Luke Wilson, Maya Rudolph, Dax Shepard</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>**ON SALE&nbsp;23rd OCT**</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>In 2005, average in every way private Joe Bowers (Luke Wilson) is selected to take part in a secret military experiment to put him in hibernation for a year along with a woman named Rita (Maya Rudolph). The slumbering duo is forgotten when the base they are stored on is closed down and are left in stasis until 2505. When they finally wake up, they discover the average intelligence of humans has decreased so much that Joe is now the smartest man in the world.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 9th November</div>                                                <li class=\"1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628367\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16659095/boyhood\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/wMwEN6VzRj4nOSnmRvDrl1cs_7PTSWhiNvfuru09a8o.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16659095/boyhood\" target=\"\">Boyhood</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2014</span>                                        <span>165mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Richard Linklater</span>                                        <span>Starring Patricia Arquette, Ethan Hawke, Ellar Coltrane</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>The joys and pitfalls of growing up are seen through the eyes of a child named Mason (Ellar Coltrane), his parents (Patricia Arquette, Ethan Hawke) and his sister (Lorelei Linklater). Vignettes, filmed with the same cast over the course of 12 years, capture family meals, road trips, birthday parties, graduations and other important milestones. Songs from Coldplay, Arcade Fire and other artists capture the time period.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 9th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628304\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/20569411/come-and-see\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/20569411.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/20569411/come-and-see\" target=\"\">Come and See</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1985</span>                                        <span>141mins</span>                                        <span>Soviet Union</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>War / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Elem Klimov</span>                                        <span>Starring Aleksei Kravchenko, Olga Mironova</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>This widely acclaimed film from Soviet director Elem Klimov is a stunning, senses-shattering plunge into the dehumanizing horrors of war. As Nazi forces encroach on his small village in present-day Belarus, teenage Flyora (Aleksei Kravchenko, in one of the screen&rsquo;s most searing depictions of anguish since Ren&eacute;e Falconetti&rsquo;s Joan of Arc) eagerly joins the Soviet resistance. Rather than the adventure and glory he envisioned, what he finds is a waking nightmare of unimaginable carnage and cruelty&mdash;rendered with a feverish, otherworldly intensity by Klimov&rsquo;s subjective camerawork and expressionistic sound design. Nearly suppressed by Soviet censors who took eight years to approve its script, Come and See is perhaps the most visceral, impossible-to-forget antiwar film ever made.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 10th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628306\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/15034200/the-holy-mountain\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/15034200.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/15034200/the-holy-mountain\" target=\"\">The Holy Mountain</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1973</span>                                        <span>115mins</span>                                        <span>Mexico</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Mind F**k</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Alejandro Jodorowsky</span>                                        <span>Starring Alejandro Jodorowsky, Horacio Salinas, Zamira Saunders</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In a corrupt, greed-fueled world, a powerful alchemist leads a messianic character and seven materialistic figures to the Holy Mountain, where they hope to achieve enlightenment.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 10th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628308\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/619980/sunset-boulevard\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/619980.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/619980/sunset-boulevard\" target=\"\">Sunset Boulevard</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1950</span>                                        <span>110mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Black Comedy / Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Billy Wilder</span>                                        <span>Starring William Holden, Gloria Swanson, Erich von Stroheim</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>An aging silent film queen refuses to accept that her stardom has ended. She hires a young screenwriter to help set up her movie comeback. The screenwriter believes he can manipulate her, but he soon finds out he is wrong. The screenwriters ambivalence about their relationship and her unwillingness to let go leads to a situation of violence, madness, and death.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 10th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628309\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617331/the-departed\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/yJPlNDmj3etYrxmSJ7S8M5I7lyNCeyYVqkNPSLANbCE.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617331/the-departed\" target=\"\">The Departed</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2006</span>                                        <span>151mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Martin Scorsese</span>                                        <span>Starring Leonardo DiCaprio, Matt Damon, Jack Nicholson, Mark Wahlberg, Martin Sheen</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>To take down South Boston's Irish Mafia, the police send in one of their own to infiltrate the underworld, not realizing the syndicate has done likewise. While an undercover cop curries favor with the mob kingpin, a career criminal rises through the police ranks. But both sides soon discover there's a mole among them.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 10th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628266\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/25247221/ms-45\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/lfV5yosA6aIBB390Rqhn1xnhD0Ppt24xD_5IdjXfDUA.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/25247221/ms-45\" target=\"\">Ms. 45</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>80mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Abel Ferrara</span>                                        <span>Starring Zoë Tamerlis, Steve Singer, Jack Thibeau, Peter Yellen</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Eerie and unforgettable, MS. 45 is an essential snapshot of New York City in the early 1980s from Abel Ferrara (DRILLER KILLER, THE ADDICTION)&mdash;one of the greatest and most unique living filmmakers on the planet. Thana (Zo&euml; Tamerlis) is a garment worker who&rsquo;s had the ultimate bad day, as she&rsquo;s assaulted twice in visceral fashion. Shocked to her core, Thana&#39;s nights become consumed by vengeful prowls through the city, which result in men winding up on the wrong end of a bullet. Knocking the DEATH WISH rip-off subgenre into a new stratosphere, MS. 45 showcases a haunting performance from Tamerlis and Ferrara&#39;s knack for transforming limited resources into genre revolutions.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em>Content Warning: Contains scenes of sexual assault that some viewers may find distressing.</em>&nbsp;<em>Further information about content and age-appropriateness for specific films can be found on&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.commonsensemedia.org/\">Common Sense Media</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/\">IMDb</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.doesthedogdie.com/\">DoesTheDogDie.com</a>, as well as through general internet searches.</em></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 11th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628323\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row live-score\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617529/the-adventures-of-prince-achmed\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/sCecmEdi7IRAOz-6suOBtgmx06hU82Lh7ygSjF-Ke8M.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617529/the-adventures-of-prince-achmed\" target=\"\">The Adventures of Prince Achmed</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1926</span>                                        <span>67mins</span>                                        <span>Germany</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Animation</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Lotte Reiniger</span>                                                                            </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><strong>This performance will feature a live score performed by <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/hugo_max_scores_silents/\">Hugo Max</a>.</strong><br />\r\n<br />\r\nLotte Reiniger&rsquo;s The Adventures of Prince Achmed is an enchanting amalgamation of stories from the Arabian Nights animated in cut paper silhouettes, an exquisite artefact of Weimar Cinema and a genre-defying experiment in melding international folk art traditions with the technical possibilities of a new medium.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTaken from The Arabian Nights, a wicked sorcerer and the beautiful prince Achmed battle one another in a series of wondrous adventures.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nPlease view <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z7rvOLnMpGM\">this&nbsp;YouTube video</a>&nbsp;for a sample of Hugo&#39;s work.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 11th November</div>                                                <li class=\"live-score\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628239\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag live-score\">LIVE SCORE</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 25th November</div>                                                <li class=\"live-score\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628240\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag live-score\">LIVE SCORE</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 70mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617485/the-odyssey\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/AoDVC-mcSmv9G8ExJ1BcGHIVmoU7f3UpgRceIrzDMeM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617485/the-odyssey\" target=\"\">The Odyssey</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>173mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Christopher Nolan</span>                                        <span>Starring Matt Damon, Tom Holland, Anne Hathaway</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Odysseus, the legendary King of Ithaca, embarks on a long and perilous journey home following the Trojan War. Throughout his voyage, he is forced to confront the whims of gods, mythological monsters, and trials that stretch both his cunning and his humanity to the breaking point.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 11th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627833\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 13th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627897\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 14th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627898\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 15th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627900\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">7:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 17th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627902\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">1:55 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627903\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 21st November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627922\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 25th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627906\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 28th November</div>                                                <li class=\"70mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627867\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 70mm\">70mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/22480264/benedetta\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/Vd2YzujGQWr7VJMLckl5u21QxNHKo_zhMhtbVKLub7A.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/22480264/benedetta\" target=\"\">Benedetta</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2021</span>                                        <span>131mins</span>                                        <span>France, Netherlands</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Film</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Paul Verhoeven</span>                                        <span>Starring Virginie Efira, Lambert Wilson, Daphne Patakia, Olivier Rabourdin, Clotilde Courau,  Olivier</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>With this orgiastic immersion in the mystic reveries of a real-life historical figure, the king of the erotic thriller Paul Verhoeven gives the nunsploitation flick a high-art makeover. Elegant, perverse, and teasingly scandalous, Benedetta critiques religious hypocrisy with an impish grin.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 12th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628326\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1300018/the-love-witch\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1300018.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1300018/the-love-witch\" target=\"\">The Love Witch</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2016</span>                                        <span>120mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Anna Biller</span>                                        <span>Starring Samantha Robinson, Jeffrey Vincent Parise, Laura Waddell</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>&ldquo;She Loved Men... To Death.&rdquo;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Addicted to love, Elaine &ndash; the love witch &ndash; casts love and sex spells to seek her perfect man, finding herself with more dead bodies than she does a long-term partner&hellip;&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A visually-striking, humorous and thought-provoking film by the continuously playful Anna Biller, The Love Witch has caused immense debate by audiences through its feminist themes. Visually drenched in 1970s fashion and cinematography, the film&acute;s style feels as magical as the love witch herself.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><em>The Love Witch is featured as part of MANEATERS, a season exploring the female supernatural on screen. The season is presented with the National Film and Television School&rsquo;s Film Studies, Programming and Curation MA.</em></span></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 12th November</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627844\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617534/have-a-gd-trip-presents-welcome-to-hell-bag-of-suck-double-feature\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/aPVr4StEsBLwyCH2wo-7VEkIxifEwNHNfnXA1MYHv9M.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617534/have-a-gd-trip-presents-welcome-to-hell-bag-of-suck-double-feature\" target=\"\">Have A Gd Trip presents Welcome To Hell &amp; Bag of Suck Double Feature</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>95mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Skateboarding Video</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jamie Thomas|Matt Eversole|Kyle Camarillo</span>                                        <span>Starring Ed Templeton, Jamie Thomas, Chad Muska, Jerry Hsu, Louie Barletta, Marc Johnson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>For one night only, <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/haveagdtrip/\"><span style=\"color:#2ecc71\">Have A Gd Trip</span></a>&nbsp;brings Skateboarding Film Club back to Prince Charles Cinema for an essential double bill celebrating two definitive eras of skate culture.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Kicking off the night is the 20th anniversary of Enjoi&rsquo;s Bag of Suck (2006)&mdash;a Transworld Video of the Year winner that balanced jaw-dropping technical progression (anchored by Jerry Hsu&rsquo;s legendary parts) with the irreverent, fun-first humour that made Enjoi an instant classic.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Followed by the 30th anniversary of Toy Machine&rsquo;s Welcome to Hell (1996)&mdash;a relentless masterpiece that set the standard for high-impact handrail skating, immortalised Jamie Thomas&rsquo;s raw style, and helped launch legends like Elissa Steamer.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Welcome to Hell</strong><br />\r\n1996 | 45mins | USA | (18) | Skateboarding Video<br />\r\nDirected by Jamie Thomas, Video introduction by Ed Templeton<br />\r\nStarring Jamie Thomas, Ed Templeton, Elissa Steamer, Chad Muska, Brian Anderson, Donny Barley<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Bag of Suck</strong><br />\r\n2006 | 50mins | USA | (18) | Skateboarding Video<br />\r\nDirected by Matt Eversole and Kyle Camarillo, Video introduction by Louie Barletta<br />\r\nStarring Jerry Hsu, Louie Barletta, Marc Johnson, Caswell Berry, Stevie Williams, Cairo Foster<br />\r\n&quot;Pandas, heavy handrails, and pure raw energy.&quot;<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTwo iconic videos, three decades of skate history, together for one night only. Rarely seen on the big screen&mdash;don&#39;t miss out.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 12th November</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628324\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">9:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617535/ricochet\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/brghPWu5-WmJZTrPXpBw6x0pQcRChqt4ZCbope-vhM0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617535/ricochet\" target=\"\">Ricochet</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1991</span>                                        <span>102mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Russell Mulcahy</span>                                        <span>Starring Denzel Washington, John Lithgow, Ice-T </span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Nick Styles, a rookie cop, sends Earl Blake, a psychotic hitman, to prison. Years later, Blake escapes prison with a well-calculated plan to seek revenge on Styles.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 13th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628329\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/609089/jason-and-the-argonauts\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/07Ek8WjcUi3eXIxpC8ulNtCOduYbpOEgUvi141r2RFM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/609089/jason-and-the-argonauts\" target=\"\">Jason and the Argonauts</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1963</span>                                        <span>104mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Adventure / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Don Chaffey</span>                                        <span>Starring Todd Armstrong, Nancy Kovack, Gary Raymond</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Jason, a fearless sailor and explorer, returns to his home land of Thessaly after a long voyage to claim his rightful throne. He learns, however, that he must first find the magical Golden Fleece. To do so, he must embark on an epic quest fraught with fantastic monsters and terrible perils.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 13th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627896\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617481/the-time-masters\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/SxejLk4uZcwAYOFSM-zePioJ2AG2V2BPGlezrzsJx0M.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617481/the-time-masters\" target=\"\">The Time Masters</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1982</span>                                        <span>79mins</span>                                        <span>France</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Animation / Sci-Fi</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by René Laloux</span>                                        <span>Starring Jean Valmont, Michel Elias, Frédéric Legros</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Directed by visionary science-fiction animator René Laloux (Fantastic Planet) and designed by the legendary Jean Giraud (a.k.a. M&oelig;bius) The Time Masters is a visually fantastic foray into existentialist space adventure. After his parents are killed on the dangerous planet Perdide, young Piel (voiced by Frédéric Legros) survives by maintaining radio contact with Jaffar (Jean Valmont), a pilot transporting the exiled Prince Matton (Yves-Marie Maurin) and Princess Belle (Monique Thierry) from their former kingdom. Jaffar seeks the help of Silbad (Michel Elias), a cheerful old-timer who knows how to circumvent Perdide&rsquo;s hazards, including brain-devouring insects and watery graves. Along the way, Jaffar and company encounter a pair of impish homunculi stowaways, identity-less angels controlled by an amorphous hive mind, and the Masters of Time, mysterious beings who can bend reality and perhaps reveal to the heroes their secret origins and destinies.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Restored in 4K in 2023 at the initiative of CITE FILMS in collaboration with the Fondazione Cineteca di Bologna and with the support of the CNC</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 13th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627817\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 19th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627818\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row sub\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617019/evangelion-death-true-the-end-of-evangelion-double-feature\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31617019.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617019/evangelion-death-true-the-end-of-evangelion-double-feature\" target=\"\">Evangelion: Death (True)² + The End of Evangelion : Double Feature</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1998</span>                                        <span>156mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Anime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Hideaki Anno</span>                                        <span>Starring Megumi Hayashibara, Megumi Ogata, Yuko Miyamura</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>EVANGELION: DEATH (TRUE)&sup2;: A recap of the first 24 episodes of Neon Genesis Evangelion. Fifteen years after the Second Impact, apathetic teen Shinji joins his father&#39;s group NERV to fight the Angels. But the truth may destroy them all.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTHE END OF EVANGELION: Concurrent theatrical ending of the TV series Neon Genesis Evangelion (1995). Seele orders an all-out attack on NERV, aiming to destroy the Evas before Gendo can trigger Third Impact and Instrumentality under his control.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 13th November</div>                                                <li class=\"sub\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627814\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag sub\">SUB</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617407/troy\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/phug56JNIijqBcg5rxE06uXU4WQGdBd1Yd1q-XzN4sM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617407/troy\" target=\"\">Troy</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2004</span>                                        <span>162mins</span>                                        <span>Mexico, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Epic</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Wolfgang Petersen</span>                                        <span>Starring Brad Pitt, Orlando Bloom, Eric Bana</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In year 1250 B.C. during the late Bronze age, two emerging nations begin to clash. Paris, the Trojan prince, convinces Helen, Queen of Sparta, to leave her husband Menelaus, and sail with him back to Troy. After Menelaus finds out that his wife was taken by the Trojans, he asks his brother Agamemnon to help him get her back. Agamemnon sees this as an opportunity for power. They set off with 1,000 ships holding 50,000 Greeks to Troy.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 14th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627899\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 am</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1122468/the-princess-bride\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1122468.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1122468/the-princess-bride\" target=\"\">The Princess Bride</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1987</span>                                        <span>98mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Romance/Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Rob Reiner</span>                                        <span>Starring Cary Elwes, Mandy Patinkin, Robin Wright</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A fairy tale adventure about a beautiful young woman and her one true love. He must find her after a long separation and save her. They must battle the evils of the mythical kingdom of Florin to be reunited with each other.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 14th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628347\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1243115/the-grand-budapest-hotel\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/9cFapMIrCtrREajcptSuCL0T_6O43jxCk27r4xuxUYI.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1243115/the-grand-budapest-hotel\" target=\"\">The Grand Budapest Hotel</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2014</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>Germany, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Wes Anderson</span>                                        <span>Starring Ralph Fiennes, F. Murray Abraham, Mathieu Amalric</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>In the 1930s, the Grand Budapest Hotel is a popular European ski resort, presided over by concierge Gustave H. (Ralph Fiennes). Zero, a junior lobby boy, becomes Gustave&#39;s friend and protege. Gustave prides himself on providing first-class service to the hotel&#39;s guests, including satisfying the sexual needs of the many elderly women who stay there. When one of Gustave&#39;s lovers dies mysteriously, Gustave finds himself the recipient of a priceless painting and the chief suspect in her murder.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 14th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628351\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3852873/predator\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/AvdGTYdYUnbWPT8CgEkGjRfLHjaBsNTdSvGXEhcYt1k.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3852873/predator\" target=\"\">Predator</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1987</span>                                        <span>107mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Action</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John McTiernan</span>                                        <span>Starring Arnold Schwarzenegger, Carl Weathers, Kevin Peter Hall</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A team of elite commandos on a secret mission in a Central American jungle come to find themselves hunted by an extraterrestrial warrior.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 14th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628352\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3527/fargo\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3527.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3527/fargo\" target=\"\">Fargo</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Crime/Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Ethan Coen|Joel Coen</span>                                        <span>Starring Frances McDormand, Steve Buscemi, William H. Macy</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Minnesota car salesman Jerry Lundegaard&#39;s inept crime falls apart due to his and his henchmen&#39;s bungling and the persistent police work of the quite pregnant Marge Gunderson.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 14th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628332\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 1st December</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627942\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11930228/labyrinth-40th-anniversary\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/1CfW40DaceKcSZAuvStM96HllFQbb_79TlyfNgFZ4CU.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/11930228/labyrinth-40th-anniversary\" target=\"\">Labyrinth - 40th Anniversary</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1986</span>                                        <span>101mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Romance / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jim Henson</span>                                        <span>Starring David Bowie, Jennifer Connelly, Jennifer Connelly and Numerous Goblins and Creatures</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Step back into the fantastical world of Jim Henson&rsquo;s Labyrinth as the beloved classic returns to cinemas for a special 40th-anniversary re-release. Starring David Bowie in one of his most entertaining film performances as the enigmatic Goblin King, this 4K re-issue brings Jim Henson&rsquo;s dazzling puppetry, imaginative landscapes, and iconic musical moments back to the big screen where they belong. Join the adventure as Sarah (Jennifer Connelly) races against time to navigate the mysterious Labyrinth and rescue her baby brother in this spellbinding cult favourite.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 15th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628357\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617536/mildred-pierce\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/zxMkxogtG3EqgTszKx9Sf9kCaetsXExYA6CxG1fTUqs.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617536/mildred-pierce\" target=\"\">Mildred Pierce</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1945</span>                                        <span>111mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Michael Curtiz</span>                                        <span>Starring Joan Crawford, Jack Carson, Zachary Scott</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When Mildred Pierce's wealthy husband leaves her for another woman, Mildred decides to raise her two daughters on her own. Despite Mildred's financial successes in the restaurant business, her oldest daughter, Veda, resents her mother for degrading their social status. In the midst of a police investigation after the death of her second husband, Mildred must evaluate her own freedom and her complicated relationship with her daughter.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 15th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628358\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2586139/highlander\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/bmonlSm5HcUCVnfk3t3qA8YG5-5d41lFPbYqvfSxUQo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2586139/highlander\" target=\"\">Highlander</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1986</span>                                        <span>116mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Action / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Russell Mulcahy</span>                                        <span>Starring Christopher Lambert, Sean Connery, Clancy Brown</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>After inexplicably surviving a mortal wound during a clan battle in the Scottish Highlands in 1536, Connor MacLeod (Christopher Lambert) is accused of witchcraft and banished from his village. Years later, he meets Ramirez (Sean Connery), a swordsman who teaches MacLeod the truth about himself: he belongs to an immortal race who can only die when the head is cut from the body.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>MacLeod fights his way through the centuries until the time of The Gathering, when the few immortals who have survived the ages will come together to fight until just one remains. In 1980s New York City the final fight is about to begin and, in the end, there can be only one...</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 15th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628366\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Monday 30th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627939\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:35 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616994/in-a-lonely-place\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31616994.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616994/in-a-lonely-place\" target=\"\">In a Lonely Place</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                                                                <span>94mins</span>                                                                                <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Nicholas Ray</span>                                        <span>Starring Humphrey Bogart, Gloria Grahame, Frank Lovejoy</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A screenwriter with a violent temper is a murder suspect until his lovely neighbor clears him. However, she soon starts to have her doubts.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 15th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628365\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/22652843/everything-everywhere-all-at-once\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/22652843.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/22652843/everything-everywhere-all-at-once\" target=\"\">Everything Everywhere All At Once</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2022</span>                                        <span>140mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Action</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Dan Kwan|Daniel Scheinert</span>                                        <span>Starring Jamie Lee Curtis, Michelle Yeoh, Stephanie Hsu, Ke Huy Quan, James Hong</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When an interdimensional rupture unravels reality, an unlikely hero must channel her newfound powers to fight bizarre and bewildering dangers from the multiverse as the fate of the world hangs in the balance.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 15th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628364\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/14753635/whiplash\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/14753635.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/14753635/whiplash\" target=\"\">Whiplash</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2014</span>                                        <span>106mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Damien Chazelle</span>                                        <span>Starring Miles Teller, J.K. Simmons, Melissa Benoist</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Andrew Neiman (Miles Teller) is an ambitious young jazz drummer, in pursuit of rising to the top of his elite music conservatory. Terence Fletcher (J.K. Simmons), an instructor known for his terrifying teaching methods, discovers Andrew and transfers the aspiring drummer into the top jazz ensemble, forever changing the young man&#39;s life. But Andrew&#39;s passion to achieve perfection quickly spirals into obsession, as his ruthless teacher pushes him to the brink of his ability and his sanity.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 16th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628371\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617531/empire-of-passion\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/27XCChLuFgGs8A__PkOdllEgN5snRlFTUqH7-cwKyOk.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617531/empire-of-passion\" target=\"\">Empire of Passion</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1978</span>                                        <span>105mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Nagisa Oshima</span>                                        <span>Starring Takahiro Tamura, Kazuko Yoshiyuki, Tatsuya Fuji</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>With an arresting mix of eroticism and horror, Oshima plunges the viewer into a nightmarish tale of guilt and retribution in Empire of Passion (Ai no borei). Set in a Japanese village at the end of the nineteenth century, the film details the emotional and physical downfall of a married woman and her younger lover following their decision to murder her husband and dump his body in a well. Empire of Passion was Oshima's only true kaidan (Japanese ghost story), and the film, a savage, unrelenting experience, earned him the best director award at the Cannes Film Festival.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 16th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628248\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:35 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 25th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628249\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3502795/taxi-driver\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3502795.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3502795/taxi-driver\" target=\"\">Taxi Driver</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1976</span>                                        <span>113mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Martin Scorsese</span>                                        <span>Starring Robert De Niro, Albert Brooks, Jodie Foster, Cybill Shepherd</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Suffering from insomnia, disturbed loner Travis Bickle (Robert De Niro) takes a job as a New York City cabbie, haunting the streets nightly, growing increasingly detached from reality as he dreams of cleaning up the filthy city. When Travis meets pretty campaign worker Betsy (Cybill Shepherd), he becomes obsessed with the idea of saving the world, first plotting to assassinate a presidential candidate, then directing his attentions toward rescuing 12-year-old prostitute Iris (Jodie Foster).</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 16th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628370\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:50 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Monday 23rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628391\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1236343/the-squid-the-whale\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/zd6V2VZXlLT2iAbVhQMMaSyGlh2Zi8Spe3dPRRR1ut8.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1236343/the-squid-the-whale\" target=\"\">The Squid &amp; The Whale</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2005</span>                                        <span>81mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Noah Baumbach</span>                                        <span>Starring Jesse Eisenberg, Jeff Daniels, Laura Linney, Owen Kline</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><em><strong>* ON SALE 23rd OCT *</strong></em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>With excruciating honesty, The Squid and the Whale chronicles the experiences of two young brothers growing up in 1980s Park Slope, Brooklyn, as they navigate the jagged contours of the divorce of their parents, both writers. The acclaimed third feature by Noah Baumbach marked a critical development for the filmmaker as he turned toward an increasingly personal style&mdash;a move that garnered him an Academy Award nomination for best original screenplay. Shot in Super 16 mm and featuring a quartet of nuanced, understated performances from Jeff Daniels, Laura Linney, Jesse Eisenberg, and Owen Kline, this comic and poignant drama, peppered with autobiographical elements, deftly captures the heartache and confusion of a fracturing family.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 16th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm 1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628305\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617033/love-exposure\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31617033.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617033/love-exposure\" target=\"\">Love Exposure</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2001</span>                                        <span>237mins</span>                                                                                <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Sion Sono</span>                                        <span>Starring Takahiro Nishijima, Hikari Mitsushima, Sakura Andô</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>The story of a teenage boy named Yu, who falls for Yoko, a girl he runs into while working as an &quot;up-skirt&quot; photographer in an offshoot of the porn industry. His attempts to woo her are complicated by a spot of cross-dressing &ndash; which convinces Yoko that she is lesbian &ndash; dalliances with kung-fu and crime, and a constant struggle with the guilt that&#39;s a legacy of his Catholic upbringing.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Contains very strong bloody violence and sex references<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 16th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628247\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">7:05 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2631771/the-warriors\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/2631771.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2631771/the-warriors\" target=\"\">The Warriors</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1979</span>                                        <span>93mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Gang</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Walter Hill</span>                                        <span>Starring Michael Beck, James Remar, Dorsey Wright</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A turf battle between New York City street gangs that rages from Coney Island to the Bronx. The Warriors are mistakenly fingered for the killing of a gang leader. Soon they have every gang in the city out to get revenge and they must make their way across the city to their own turf.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 17th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628374\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9888606/escape-from-new-york\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/9888606.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9888606/escape-from-new-york\" target=\"\">Escape from New York</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>99mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Action</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Carpenter</span>                                        <span>Starring Kurt Russell, Lee Van Cleef, Adrienne Barbeau, Donald Pleasence, Harry Dean Stanton, Ernest Borgnine</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In 1997, a major war between the United States and the Soviet Union is concluding, and the entire island of Manhattan has been converted into a giant maximum security prison. When Air Force One is hijacked and crashes into the island, the president (Donald Pleasence) is taken hostage by a group of inmates. Snake Plissken (Kurt Russell), a former Special Forces soldier turned criminal, is recruited to retrieve the president in exchange for his own freedom.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 17th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628375\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1390477/before-sunrise\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1390477.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1390477/before-sunrise\" target=\"\">Before Sunrise</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1995</span>                                        <span>101mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Romance/Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Richard Linklater</span>                                        <span>Starring Ethan Hawke, Julie Delpy, Andrea Eckert</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>On his way to Vienna, American Jesse (Ethan Hawke) meets Celine (Julie Delpy), a student returning to Paris. After long conversations forge a surprising connection between them, Jesse convinces Celine to get off the train with him in Vienna. Since his flight to the U.S. departs the next morning and he has no money for lodging, they wander the city together, taking in the experiences of Vienna and each other. As the night progresses, their bond makes separating in the morning a difficult choice.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 17th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628373\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/30992970/laura\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/30992970.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/30992970/laura\" target=\"\">Laura</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1944</span>                                        <span>88mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Otto Preminger</span>                                        <span>Starring Clifton Webb, Dana Andrews, Dorothy Adams, Gene Tierney, James Flavin, Judith Anderson, Vincent Price</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A police detective falls in love with the woman whose murder he is investigating.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 17th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628334\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/618352/no-country-for-old-men\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/618352.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/618352/no-country-for-old-men\" target=\"\">No Country For Old Men</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2007</span>                                        <span>122mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Ethan Coen|Joel Coen</span>                                        <span>Starring Tommy Lee Jones, Josh Brolin, Javier Bardem</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>While out hunting, Llewelyn Moss (Josh Brolin) finds the grisly aftermath of a drug deal. Though he knows better, he cannot resist the cash left behind and takes it with him. The hunter becomes the hunted when a merciless killer named Chigurh (Javier Bardem) picks up his trail. Also looking for Moss is Sheriff Bell (Tommy Lee Jones), an aging lawman who reflects on a changing world and a dark secret of his own, as he tries to find and protect Moss.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 18th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628341\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 29th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627876\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16751003/out-of-the-past\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/l6j9fHoQ1Jw90gaHxzemvapPIeJgSYvcxHlnQXSdTAk.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16751003/out-of-the-past\" target=\"\">Out of the Past</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1947</span>                                        <span>97mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jacques Tourneur</span>                                        <span>Starring Kirk Douglas, Robert Mitchum, Jane Greer</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A private eye escapes his past to run a gas station in a small town, but his past catches up with him. Now he must return to the big city world of danger, corruption, double crosses, and duplicitous dames.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 18th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628340\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:55 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/6018846/the-big-lebowski\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/6018846.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/6018846/the-big-lebowski\" target=\"\">The Big Lebowski</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1998</span>                                        <span>117mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Ethan Coen|Joel Coen</span>                                        <span>Starring Jeff Bridges, Julianne Moore, John Goodman</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Jeff \"The Dude\" Lebowski, mistaken for a millionaire of the same name, seeks restitution for his ruined rug and enlists his bowling buddies to help get it.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 18th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628336\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23457193/daisies-sedmikrsky\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/23457193.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/23457193/daisies-sedmikrsky\" target=\"\">Daisies (Sedmikrásky)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1966</span>                                        <span>76mins</span>                                        <span>Czechoslovakia, Slovakia</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Vera Chytilová</span>                                        <span>Starring Jitka Cerhová, Ivana Karbanová</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>After realizing that all world is spoiled, Marie and Marie are committed to be spoiled themselves. They rip off older men, feast in lavish meals and do all kinds of mischief. But what is all this leading to?</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 18th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628377\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617017/music-video-preservation-society-with-special-guest-tim-pope\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/nmx5yUyww-suYAq3kx0Trv2SnKu5QpS06twRztu0nXs.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617017/music-video-preservation-society-with-special-guest-tim-pope\" target=\"\">Music Video Preservation Society with special guest Tim Pope</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                                                                <span>135mins</span>                                                                                <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Music Video</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                                                                                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Music Video Preservation Society, the big screen celebration of the art and cultural impact of music videos returns to the big screen at the Prince Charles Cinema on Wednesday November 18th, with special guest, filmmaker Tim Pope (director of classic videos for The Cure, Neil Young, The The, Bowie, etc).</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 18th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628378\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/15480669/vertigo\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/15480669.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/15480669/vertigo\" target=\"\">Vertigo</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1958</span>                                        <span>128mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Thriller/Suspense</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Alfred Hitchcock</span>                                        <span>Starring James Stewart, Kim Novak, Barbara Bel Geddes</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A former San Francisco police detective juggles wrestling with his personal demons and becoming obsessed with the hauntingly beautiful woman he has been hired to trail, who may be deeply disturbed.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 19th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628338\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/26595713/the-piano\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/_ng4wKP5-x1ShNu5s8n-qU3YkWVRE_D0xLgFjH3oGpM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/26595713/the-piano\" target=\"\">The Piano</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1993</span>                                        <span>121mins</span>                                        <span>Australia, France, New Zealand</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Romance/Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jane Campion</span>                                        <span>Starring Holly Hunter, Sam Neill, Harvey Keitel, Anna Paquin, Kerry Walker, Genevieve Lemon</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>In the mid-19th century a mute woman is sent to New Zealand along with her young daughter and prized piano for an arranged marriage to a farmer, but is soon lusted after by a farm worker.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 19th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628380\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617530/byzantium\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/93ReRvUeQi92vYR_i_IKZKek9q7ZvH2WUziqKxZxvZo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617530/byzantium\" target=\"\">Byzantium</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2012</span>                                        <span>118mins</span>                                        <span>Belgium, Ireland, UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Neil Jordan</span>                                        <span>Starring Saoirse Ronan, Gemma Arterton, Sam Riley</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p><em>&ldquo;We are a brotherhood. There are no women amongst us&rdquo;&nbsp;</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Hunted for two centuries, Clara and Eleanor Webb are the only female vampires alive: a mother who feeds on human blood and will go to any lengths to survive, and her daughter who despises what she is and tries to live a moral life. Forced to find refuge in a run-down coastal hotel, they realise that they can not hide forever; not when their past and secrets are coming back to haunt them.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Blood waterfalls, razor-sharp claws and cults of knowledge; from the director of Interview with the Vampire (1994), Byzantium is deliciously gothic, seductively atmospheric, and inescapably tragic. A must-watch title in the vampire genre, Neil Jordan depicts vampire lore in a contemporary way while staying true to its archaic themes.&nbsp;<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><em>Byzantium is featured as part of MANEATERS, a season exploring the female supernatural on screen. The season is presented with the National Film and Television School&rsquo;s Film Studies, Programming and Curation MA.</em></span></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 19th November</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628245\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3505/ten-years-of-monkey-tennis-with-peter-serafinowicz\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/wtmwGkpu07rzMdK_ajq7CSlNt6C8GqKwRxCCKvYg4jU.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3505/ten-years-of-monkey-tennis-with-peter-serafinowicz\" target=\"\">Ten Years of Monkey Tennis (with Peter Serafinowicz)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2026</span>                                        <span>90mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Live Podcast</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Monkey Tennis</span>                                        <span>Starring Adam Brooks, Nick Alder, Tom Dark, Tom Stabb, Jed Shepherd</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>&quot;One of the best TV and film podcasts&quot; - The Telegraph</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Join the hosts of chart-topping, award-winning Alan Partridge fan podcast Monkey Tennis as they celebrate a full decade of dissecting, discussing and celebrating Norwich&#39;s finest broadcaster, joined by very special guest, BAFTA nominee, comedy legend and Partridge alumni <strong>Peter Serafinowicz</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This special intimate one-off anniversary live podcast recording sees your four dalendless hosts return to the scene of their first ever live show, to recognise and revel in Alan Gordon Partridge&#39;s glory. They&#39;ll also be speaking to star of I&#39;m Alan Partridge (as well as Guardians of the Galaxy, Amandaland, Parks &amp; Recreation, Shaun of the Dead, Spaced and 100+ more), <strong>Peter Serafinowicz</strong>, about his epic career and his time as Alan&#39;s antagonist and lover of American things, Tex.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In the meantime, catch up on over 150 episodes of the Monkey Tennis podcast, covering almost everything Alan&#39;s ever done, at <a href=\"http://podfollow.com/monkeytennis\">podfollow.com/monkeytennis</a></p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 19th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31626392\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/17436234/crash-1996\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/z1em39Ju2DWJV4vP-lj58n-wQpvLzA9kk1C2OnV3nww.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/17436234/crash-1996\" target=\"\">Crash (1996)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1996</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>Canada</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Erotic / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by David Cronenberg</span>                                        <span>Starring James Spader, Holly Hunter, Elias Koteas</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Technology and sexuality meet in a head-on collision in David Cronenberg&#39;s controversial adaptation of writer J.G. Ballard&#39;s hugely transgressive 1973 novel, starring James Spader and Holly Hunter.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Spader stars as James Ballard, a film producer whose deviant sexual desires are awakened by a near-fatal automobile accident with Dr. Helen Remington (Hunter). Soon, the pair, alongside Ballard&#39;s wife Catherine (Deborah Kara Unger), are drawn into an underground world of car crash fetishism presided over by renegade scientist Vaughan (Elias Koteas). Danger, sex and death become entwined as eroticism and technology join together in a disturbing, deadly union.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628381\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/624770/a-streetcar-named-desire\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/624770.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/624770/a-streetcar-named-desire\" target=\"\">A Streetcar Named Desire</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1951</span>                                        <span>125mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Elia Kazan</span>                                        <span>Starring Kim Hunter, Marlon Brando, Vivien Leigh</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Based on the play by Tennessee Williams, this renowned drama follows troubled former schoolteacher Blanche DuBois (Vivien Leigh) as she leaves small-town Mississippi and moves in with her sister, Stella Kowalski (Kim Hunter), and her husband, Stanley (Marlon Brando), in New Orleans. Blanche's flirtatious Southern-belle presence causes problems for Stella and Stanley, who already have a volatile relationship, leading to even greater conflict in the Kowalski household.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628383\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617537/my-dinner-with-andre\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/C6lyx7TXbdizmycfUaEYSGomKRisxCZJZe0u0DCw4P4.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617537/my-dinner-with-andre\" target=\"\">My Dinner with Andre</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>110mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Louis Malle</span>                                        <span>Starring Andre Gregory, Wallace Shawn, Jean Lenauer</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Two legends of the theatre discuss life, the universe and pretty much everything else in this hugely admired conversation piece from Louis Malle.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Acclaimed playwrights, essayists and actors Wallace Shawn and Andr&eacute; Gregory meet at Caf&eacute; des Artistes in Manhattan. Initially, Gregory dominates the conversation with his exploits over the course of the previous five years, from working with theatre groups in Europe to traveling through the Sahara. Shawn&rsquo;s response is to ground the conversation in the virtues of everyday life &ndash; that its pleasures can be obtained through the simplest acts. Malle&rsquo;s camera is the third member of the group and we are given a rare insight into the minds of two fascinating &ndash; albeit slightly fictional &ndash; people. My Dinner with Andre is a celebration of friendship, conversation and the pleasures of a cup of coffee.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628382\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617482/gandahar\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/Z_DgEE4p5K47lME5WqsD9ZKP9lAmjgvfdFoFZhLzK3s.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617482/gandahar\" target=\"\">Gandahar</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1987</span>                                        <span>83mins</span>                                        <span>France</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Animation / Sci-Fi</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by René Laloux</span>                                        <span>Starring Catherine Chevallier, Pierre-Marie Escourrou, Anny Duperey</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>An entire civilisation must confront its destiny in alternative-animation pioneer René Laloux's final feature, a cult classic of mind-bending science fiction. In a distant world, a merciless army of automata attacks Gandahar, turning its peace-loving people to stone. Hoping to discover the source of these Men of Metal, a council of matriarchs enlists the brave yet inexperienced warrior Sylvain (Pierre-Marie Escourro), who, while journeying through his planet's outer regions, teams up with the Deformed, a race cast out from Gandahar after failed science experiments rendered them mutants. Soon, Sylvain learns that a gargantuan brain called Metamorphis (Georges Wilson) is responsible for his utopian society's strife and—together with the beautiful Airelle (Catherine Chevallier)—travels through time to defeat him, in the process risking their lives and Gandahar's very existence. Featuring stunningly surreal creatures and wondrously bizarre environments designed by renowned comic-book artist Caza, Gandahar is a visceral, visionary head-trip in which animation opens a gateway to the furthest reaches of the imagination.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627819\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Monday 23rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627820\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627821\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/6162142/the-prestige\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/6162142.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/6162142/the-prestige\" target=\"\">The Prestige</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2006</span>                                        <span>130mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Psychological Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Christopher Nolan</span>                                        <span>Starring Christian Bale, Hugh Jackman, Scarlett Johansson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Period thriller set in Edwardian London where two rival magicians, partners until the tragic death of an assistant during a show, feud bitterly after one of them performs the ultimate magic trick - teleportation. His rival tries desperately to uncover the secret of his routine, experimenting with dangerous new science as his quest takes him to the brink of insanity and jeopardises the lives of everyone around the pair.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 20th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627919\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k sub\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4535195/arrietty\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/3evviWBTxzYOYqjozi2-LVF2taEsIusT3d7ZDqQhjt0.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/4535195/arrietty\" target=\"\">Arrietty</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2010</span>                                        <span>94mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Anime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Hiromasa Yonebayashi</span>                                        <span>Starring Mirai Shida, Tomokazu Miura, Shinobu Ohtake</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>From the creators of Spirited Away and Ponyo, and Academy Award&reg;-nominated director Hiromasa Yonebayashi, comes a gorgeous and adventure-filled adaptation of The Borrowers, one of the most beloved children&rsquo;s books of all time.<br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\nIn a secret world hidden beneath the floorboards, tiny people called Borrowers live out of sight of humans. But when brave Arrietty is out gathering supplies, she is discovered by Shawn, a human boy, and they begin to form a friendship that blossoms into a heartwarming adventure.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 21st November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k sub\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628246\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:35 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span><span class=\"tag sub\">SUB</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 3rd December</div>                                                <li class=\"4k sub\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627953\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span><span class=\"tag sub\">SUB</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1865764/double-indemnity\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/1865764.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/1865764/double-indemnity\" target=\"\">Double Indemnity</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1944</span>                                        <span>107mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Billy Wilder</span>                                        <span>Starring Barbara St, Barbara Stanwyck, Edward G. Robinson, Fred MacMurray</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>In this classic film noir, insurance salesman Walter Neff (Fred MacMurray) gets roped into a murderous scheme when he falls for the sensual Phyllis Dietrichson (Barbara Stanwyck), who is intent on killing her husband (Tom Powers) and living off the fraudulent accidental death claim. Prompted by the late Mr. Dietrichson&#39;s daughter, Lola (Jean Heather), insurance investigator Barton Keyes (Edward G. Robinson) looks into the case, and gradually begins to uncover the sinister truth.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 21st November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628342\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/17389471/tenet\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/ViilFY4PohkDzQeYqKPMrnrTiWcW8Z21LcKh3orSolM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/17389471/tenet\" target=\"\">Tenet</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2020</span>                                        <span>150mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Christopher Nolan</span>                                        <span>Starring John David Washington, Robert Pattinson, Kenneth Branagh, Michael Caine, Elizabeth Debicki</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Armed with only one word—Tenet—and fighting for the survival of the entire world, the Protagonist journeys through a twilight world of international espionage on a mission that will unfold in something beyond real time.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 21st November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627923\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616877/cure\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/31616877.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616877/cure\" target=\"\">Cure</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1997</span>                                        <span>111mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Kiyoshi Kurosawa</span>                                        <span>Starring Kôji Yakusho, Masato Hagiwara, Tsuyoshi Ujiki</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A detective starts spiraling out of control when a wave of gruesome murders with seemingly similar bizarre circumstances are sweeping Tokyo.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 21st November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628343\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2666249/blue-velvet\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/2666249.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2666249/blue-velvet\" target=\"\">Blue Velvet</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1986</span>                                        <span>121mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Neo Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by David Lynch</span>                                        <span>Starring Kyle MacLachlan, Dennis Hopper, Isabella Rossellini</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>College student Jeffrey Beaumont (Kyle MacLachlan) returns home after his father has a stroke. When he discovers a severed ear in an abandoned field, Beaumont teams up with detective&#39;s daughter Sandy Williams (Laura Dern) to solve the mystery. They believe beautiful lounge singer Dorothy Vallens (Isabella Rossellini) may be connected with the case, and Beaumont finds himself becoming drawn into her dark, twisted world, where he encounters sexually depraved psychopath Frank Booth (Dennis Hopper)</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 21st November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628385\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617491/clash-of-the-titans\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/pOkiDC6Q7hQ-LliQ30-xQlCygY71Utcawd2xZkgJq4c.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617491/clash-of-the-titans\" target=\"\">Clash of the Titans</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>118mins</span>                                        <span>UK, USA</span>                                        <span>(12)</span>                                        <span>Adventure / Fantasy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Desmond Davis</span>                                        <span>Starring Harry Hamlin, Judi Bowker, Burgess Meredith, Laurence Olivier, Maggie Smith</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>To win the right to marry his love, the beautiful princess Andromeda, and fulfil his destiny, half-God-half-mortal Perseus must complete various tasks including taming Pegasus, capturing Medusa's head and battling the feared Kraken.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 22nd November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627909\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">11:45 am</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/5906838/insomnia\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/8sZYOR45qZl6LuxC0hgPOBeXTKyLH0Ko-6vFDTiF7Eo.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/5906838/insomnia\" target=\"\">Insomnia</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2002</span>                                        <span>118mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Christopher Nolan</span>                                        <span>Starring Al Pacino, Robin Williams, Hilary Swank</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Under the glare of the permanent Alaska sun, two veteran Los Angeles police officers close in on their suspect in the murder of a teenage girl. But when officer Will Dormer (Al Pacino) accidentally shoots his partner, their murder suspect, reclusive novelist Walter Finch (Robin Williams), witnesses the shooting--and blackmails Dormer. Now, as an idealistic local detective (Hillary Swank) investigates the case, and the stakes rise, Dormer's sanity begins to falter.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 22nd November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627910\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13081888/dead-poets-society\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/13081888.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13081888/dead-poets-society\" target=\"\">Dead Poets Society</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1989</span>                                        <span>129mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Comedy / Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Peter Weir</span>                                        <span>Starring Ethan Hawke, Robin Williams, Robert Sean Leonard</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>A new English teacher, John Keating (Robin Williams), is introduced to an all-boys preparatory school that is known for its ancient traditions and high standards. He uses unorthodox methods to reach out to his students, who face enormous pressures from their parents and the school. With Keating&#39;s help, students Neil Perry (Robert Sean Leonard), Todd Anderson (Ethan Hawke) and others learn to break out of their shells, pursue their dreams and seize the day.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 22nd November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628388\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:10 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9639087/ikiru\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/9639087.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/9639087/ikiru\" target=\"\">Ikiru</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1952</span>                                        <span>143mins</span>                                        <span>Japan</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Drama</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Akira Kurosawa</span>                                        <span>Starring Takashi Shimura, Nobuo Kaneko, Shin'ichi Himori</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Mr. Watanabe suddenly finds that he has terminal cancer. He vows to make his final days meaningful. His attempts to communicate his anguish to his son and daughter-in-law lead only to heartbreak. Finally, inspired by an unselfish co-worker, he turns his efforts to bringing happiness to others by building a playground in a dreary slum neighborhood. When the park is finally completed, he is able to face death with peaceful acceptance.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 23rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628398\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/8379700/speed-racer\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/8379700.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/8379700/speed-racer\" target=\"\">Speed Racer</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2008</span>                                        <span>135mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Action/Adventure</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Lana Wachowski|Lilly Wachowski</span>                                        <span>Starring Christina Ricci, Emile Hirsch, Matthew Fox</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Born into a family business of race cars, Speed Racer (Emile Hirsch) is one of the track's hot stars. Sitting at the wheel of his Mach 5, he consistently deflates the competition. When Speed turns down an offer from the head of Royalton Industries, he uncovers a secret. Powerful moguls fix the races to boost profits. Hoping to beat the executive, Speed enters the same arduous cross-country race that killed his brother.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 23rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628396\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:55 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 1-mem\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617538/brute-force\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/K5UAmpYXw6tU9RGgVtWJgycQX2iXmoFn4jqvcgV5pE8.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31617538/brute-force\" target=\"\">Brute Force</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1947</span>                                        <span>98mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(12A)</span>                                        <span>Film Noir</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jules Dassin</span>                                        <span>Starring Burt Lancaster, Hume Cronyn, Charles Bickford</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>* ON SALE 23rd OCT *<br />\r\n<br />\r\nTimeworn Joe Collins and his fellow inmates live under the heavy thumb of the sadistic, power-tripping guard Captain Munsey. Only Collins&#39; dreams of escape keep him going, but how can he possibly bust out of Munsey&#39;s chains?</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Monday 23rd November</div>                                                <li class=\"1-mem\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628394\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 1-mem\">£1 MEM</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19307195/the-fly-1986\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/7u2ZdwQIlINj55u0DbBHDpk6lwsG3sjV7R9gOI0j0r4.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/19307195/the-fly-1986\" target=\"\">The Fly (1986)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1986</span>                                        <span>96mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Sci-Fi / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by David Cronenberg</span>                                        <span>Starring Jeff Goldblum, Geena Davis, Joy Boushel, Les Carlson, Gordon Chuvalo</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>When scientist Seth Brundle completes his teleportation device, he decides to test its abilities on himself. Unbeknownst to him, a housefly slips in during the process, leading to a merger of man and insect. Initially, Brundle appears to have undergone a successful teleportation, but the fly's cells begin to take over his body. As he becomes increasingly fly-like, Brundle's girlfriend is horrified as the person she once loved deteriorates into a monster.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 24th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628400\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/17956995/peeping-tom\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/X_tQ8k0hlVYgAKdJcX3lJPEHGi-uGXhUobuYVjJElPM.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/17956995/peeping-tom\" target=\"\">Peeping Tom</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1960</span>                                        <span>101mins</span>                                        <span>UK</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Crime / Thriller</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Michael Powell</span>                                        <span>Starring Karlheinz Böhm, Anna Massey, Moira Shearer</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Loner Mark Lewis works at a film studio during the day and, at night, takes racy photographs of women. Also he's making a documentary on fear, which involves recording the reactions of victims as he murders them. He befriends Helen, the daughter of the family living in the apartment below his, and he tells her vaguely about the movie he is making.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 24th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628344\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/5909871/dirty-rotten-scoundrels\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/yguvbQBuxx1wo-99Y0gRRHDzBGe4yezR9ZCandMwLEg.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/5909871/dirty-rotten-scoundrels\" target=\"\">Dirty Rotten Scoundrels</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1988</span>                                        <span>110mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Comedy/Crime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Frank Oz</span>                                        <span>Starring Steve Martin, Michael Caine, Glenne Headly</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Two con men try to settle their rivalry by betting on who can swindle a young American heiress out of fifty thousand dollars first.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 24th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628401\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:40 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16654545/thief\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/16654545.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16654545/thief\" target=\"\">Thief</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1981</span>                                        <span>122mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Crime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Michael Mann</span>                                        <span>Starring James Caan, Tuesday Weld, Willie Nelson</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A highly skilled jewel thief, Frank (James Caan) longs to leave his dangerous trade and settle down with his girlfriend, Jessie (Tuesday Weld). Eager to make one last big score in order to begin living a legitimate life, Frank reluctantly associates with Leo (Robert Prosky), a powerful gangster. Unfortunately for Frank, Leo wants to keep him in his employ, resulting in a tense showdown when he finally tries to give up his criminal activities once and for all.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 24th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627931\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/26050305/miami-vice\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/26050305.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/26050305/miami-vice\" target=\"\">Miami Vice</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2006</span>                                        <span>123mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Action / Crime</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Michael Mann</span>                                        <span>Starring Colin Farrell, Gong Li, Jamie Foxx, Justin Theroux, Naomie Harris, Ciarán Hinds</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>A case involving drug lords and murder in South Florida takes a personal turn for undercover detectives Sonny Crockett (Colin Farrell) and Ricardo Tubbs (Jamie Foxx). Unorthodox Crockett gets involved romantically with the Chinese-Cuban wife of a trafficker of arms and drugs, while Tubbs deals with an assault on those he loves.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Tuesday 24th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627930\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">8:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2585925/playtime\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/2585925.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2585925/playtime\" target=\"\">Playtime</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1967</span>                                        <span>123mins</span>                                        <span>France, Italy</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Comedy Genius</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Jacques Tati</span>                                        <span>Starring Jacques Tati, Barbara Dennek, Rita Maiden</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Clumsy Monsieur Hulot (Jacques Tati) finds himself perplexed by the intimidating complexity of a gadget-filled Paris. He attempts to meet with a business contact but soon becomes lost. His roundabout journey parallels that of an American tourist (Barbara Dennek), and as they weave through the inventive urban environment, they intermittently meet, developing an interest in one another. They eventually get together at a chaotic restaurant, along with several other quirky characters.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 25th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628405\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16649791/night-moves-1975\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/16649791.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/16649791/night-moves-1975\" target=\"\">Night Moves [1975]</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1975</span>                                        <span>100mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Thriller / Mystery</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Arthur Penn</span>                                        <span>Starring Gene Hackman, Jennifer Warren, Edward Binns</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Hard-nosed private investigator Harry Moseby (Gene Hackman), to distract himself from a rapidly deteriorating marriage, takes a case from an aging B-movie queen (Janet Ward) to locate her runaway daughter, Delly (Melanie Griffith). His search takes him to the Florida Keys, where the girl has been hiding out with her stepfather, Tom (John Crawford), and Tom's lover, Paula (Jennifer Warren). Harry initiates an affair with Paula and soon learns the case is more complex than he first assessed it.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Wednesday 25th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628404\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">3:20 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/8924103/west-side-story-1961\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/8924103.jpeg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/8924103/west-side-story-1961\" target=\"\">West Side Story (1961)</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1961</span>                                        <span>153mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(PG)</span>                                        <span>Musical / Romance</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Robert Wise|Jerome Robbins</span>                                        <span>Starring Natalie Wood, George Chakiris, Richard Beymer</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Two youngsters from rival New York City gangs fall in love, but tensions between their respective friends build toward tragedy.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628409\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:25 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 4k\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3721500/blade-runner-the-final-cut\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3721500.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3721500/blade-runner-the-final-cut\" target=\"\">Blade Runner : The Final Cut</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1982</span>                                        <span>118mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Science Fiction</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Ridley Scott</span>                                        <span>Starring Harrison Ford, Sean Young, Rutger Hauer</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Deckard (Harrison Ford) is forced by the police Boss (M. Emmet Walsh) to continue his old job as Replicant Hunter. His assignment: eliminate four escaped Replicants from the colonies who have returned to Earth. Before starting the job, Deckard goes to the Tyrell Corporation and he meets Rachel (Sean Young), a Replicant girl he falls in love with.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"4k\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628406\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 4k\">4K</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2335055/the-last-waltz\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/2335055.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/2335055/the-last-waltz\" target=\"\">The Last Waltz</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1978</span>                                        <span>116mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Documentary</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Martin Scorsese</span>                                        <span>Starring Robbie Robertson, Neil Young, Bob Dylan, Muddy Waters</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Seventeen years after joining forces as the backing band for rockabilly cult hero Ronnie Hawkins, Canadian roots rockers The Band call it quits with a lavish farewell show at San Francisco&#39;s Winterland Ballroom on Nov. 25, 1976. Filmed by Martin Scorsese, this documentary features standout performances by rock legends such as Bob Dylan, Neil Young, Van Morrison, Eric Clapton, Joni Mitchell and Muddy Waters, as well as interviews tracing the group&#39;s history and discussing road life.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628407\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row intro\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13006809/ginger-snaps\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://cdn.taposapp.com/poster/600x900/FbBrdUjypmLV9eCkjETRiIaFMmgj8WupQRTN4S8nw_Q.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13006809/ginger-snaps\" target=\"\">Ginger Snaps</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>2000</span>                                        <span>108mins</span>                                        <span>Canada</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Teen / Horror</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Fawcett</span>                                        <span>Starring Emily Perkins, Katharine Isabelle, Kris Lemche</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>&ldquo;I get this ache... And I, I thought it was for sex, but it&#39;s to tear everything to fucking pieces.&rdquo;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A wild and bloodthirsty hound has ravaged through the small town of Bailey Downs, attacking the neighbourhood&#39;s pet dogs. When the two teenage outcasts, the Fitzgerald sisters, stumble upon the creature one night, their lives change forever as Ginger is bitten, and her body starts to change.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>A true feast of practical effects, 2000s grunge, and snappy one-liners; Ginger Snaps has been credited in hindsight as a predecessor to the &ldquo;maneater&rdquo; supernatural woman most famously seen in Jennifer&acute;s Body (2009). A coming-of-age story told in a fresh perspective; for maybe the true terror lies in growing up, or maybe it lies in the bloodthirsty hound who calls herself your sister.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\"><em>Ginger Snaps is featured as part of MANEATERS, a season exploring the female supernatural on screen. The season is presented with the National Film and Television School&rsquo;s Film Studies, Programming and Curation MA.</em></span><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"intro\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627847\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">6:15 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag intro\">Intro</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row 35mm\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3639995/planes-trains-automobiles\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/3639995.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/3639995/planes-trains-automobiles\" target=\"\">Planes, Trains &amp; Automobiles</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1987</span>                                        <span>92mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(15)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by John Hughes</span>                                        <span>Starring John Candy, Laila Robins, Steve Martin</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>Easily excitable Neal Page (Steve Martin) is somewhat of a control freak. Trying to get home to Chicago to spend Thanksgiving with his wife (Laila Robins) and kids, his flight is rerouted to a distant city in Kansas because of a freak snowstorm, and his sanity begins to fray. Worse yet, he is forced to bunk up with talkative Del Griffith (John Candy), whom he finds extremely annoying. Together they must overcome the insanity of holiday travel to reach their intended destination.</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Thursday 26th November</div>                                                <li class=\"35mm\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31628408\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">9:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag 35mm\">35mm</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616758/a-confucian-confusion\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/sDEPrUoBf52AISJd5liP47ofKzp.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/31616758/a-confucian-confusion\" target=\"\">A Confucian Confusion</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1994</span>                                        <span>125mins</span>                                        <span>Taiwan</span>                                        <span>(18)</span>                                        <span>Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Edward Yang</span>                                        <span>Starring Chen Shiang-chyi, Chen Yi-wen, Danny Deng</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p>Art versus commerce, friendship versus status, independence versus conformity—values clash and collide in Edward Yang's study of an increasingly Westernized country heading into the twenty-first century without moral guideposts. Moving from breakout hit A Brighter Summer Day's investigation of the past to a critical survey of the present, A Confucian Confusion charts the tangled web of emotional and professional manipulations among a group of young urbanites. At its center is Molly (Ni Shu-chun), director of a floundering public-relations firm. Alienated by the childish fiancé (Bosen Wang) who bankrolls her enterprise—and frustrated by the demands of an assistant, Qiqi (Chen Shiang-chyi), and her own fiancé, Ming (Wang Wei-ming)—Molly lashes out at everyone in her path and threatens to dismantle the company altogether. Meanwhile (amid several other subplots), Molly's talk-show-host sister (Chen Li-mei) attempts to dissuade her separated husband from continuing to write a dark novel about the return of Confucius to a jaded modern society. Injecting comedic elements into his patented brand of earnest soul-searching, Yang finds humor as well as pathos in the desperate behavior of a lost and lonely generation.</p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 27th November</div>                                                <li class=\"\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627862\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">12:00 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\">                                                    </div>\n                                                </li>                                        </ul>          \n                                    </div>\n                                </div></div>\n                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"jacro-event movie-tabs row sing-along\">\n                        <div class=\"col-md-12 col-xs-12\">\n                            <div class=\"film_list-outer\">\n                                <div class=\"film_img\">\n                                    <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13427144/the-muppet-christmas-carol\">\n                                       <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"filmimg\" src=\"https://posters-uk.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/PRILON/13427144.jpg\" class=\"img-responsive\" width=\"150\" height=\"210\" onError=\"this.onerror=null;this.src='https://princecharlescinema.com/wp-content/plugins/jacro-plugin/images/default.png';\">\n                                    </a>\n                                </div>\n                                <div class=\"jacrofilm-list-content\">\n                                    <a class=\"liveeventtitle\" href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/film/13427144/the-muppet-christmas-carol\" target=\"\">The Muppet Christmas Carol</a>\n                                    <div class=\"running-time\">\n                                        <span>1992</span>                                        <span>89mins</span>                                        <span>USA</span>                                        <span>(U)</span>                                        <span>Musical / Comedy</span>                                    </div>\n                                    <div class=\"film-info\">\n                                        <span>Directed by Brian Henson</span>                                        <span>Starring Frank Oz, Dave Goelz, Michael Caine, Steve Whitmire, Meredith Braun</span>                                    </div>\n                                                                        <div class=\"jacro-formatted-text\"><p><p>&#39;Tis the season for love, laughter, and one of the most cherished stories of all time! Join Kermit the Frog, Miss Piggy, and all the hilarious Muppets in this merry, magical version of Charles Dickens&#39; classic tale. Academy Award&reg; winner Michael Caine (Best Supporting Actor) gives a performance that&#39;s anything but &quot;bah, humbug!&quot; as greedy, penny-pinching Ebenezer Scrooge. One fateful Christmas Eve, Scrooge is visited by the Ghosts of Christmas Past, Present, and Future. Together with kind, humble Bob Cratchit (Kermit the Frog) and his family, the Spirits open Scrooge&#39;s eyes -- and his heart -- to the true meaning of Christmas. Filled with original music and dazzling special effects, THE MUPPET CHRISTMAS CAROL will become a holiday tradition your family will treasure all the days of the year.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nFeaturing the film&rsquo;s famous long-lost song &lsquo;When Love is Gone&rsquo;!<br />\r\n<br />\r\n------<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<em><strong>As always you can expect SING ALONG&nbsp;performances of this new version of THE MUPPET CHRISTMAS CAROL this Christmas - and now we don&#39;t need to pretend that we weren&#39;t going to just play the lost scene regardless!</strong></em> Performances will feature a Hosted Pre-Show with our very own Father Christmas, where you will be prepped on what to do throughout the film. Costumes&nbsp;aren&#39;t mandatory, but &#39;Tis the season, and we love seeing you dressed up in your favourite Christmas Jumpers! All this, and a few more surprises up our sleeves, makes this one of the must-see events this Christmas!<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you&#39;re wanting to Sing Along with The Muppet Christmas Carol, simply book for the performances marked SING ALONG [it&#39;s next to the start time]. All other screenings will be regular performances, and nothing will be written next to the start time.&nbsp;</p></p></div>\n                                    <div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n                                </div>\n                                <!--- show time --->\n                                                                    <div class=\"performance-list-items-outer\">\n                                        <ul class=\"performance-list-items\"><div class=\"heading\">Friday 27th November</div>                                                <li class=\"sing-along\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627853\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:30 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag sing-along\">Sing Along</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Saturday 28th November</div>                                                <li class=\"sing-along\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627854\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">5:45 pm</span>\n                                                        </a>                                                    <div class=\"movietag\"><span class=\"tag sing-along\">Sing Along</span>                                                    </div>\n                                                </li><div class=\"heading\">Sunday 29th November</div>                                                <li class=\"sing-along\">\n                                                    \n                                                                                                           <a href=\"https://princecharlescinema.com/prince-charles-cinema/booknow/31627855\" class=\"film_book_button\">\n                                                            <span class=\"hover\">Book</span>\n                                                            <span class=\"time\">2:15 pm</span>\n                                                 